// Detailed navigation extends the existing objectives so older progress keeps its meaning.
function detail(ch,index,rows){const c=C.find(c=>c.id===ch);if(!c.details)c.details={};c.details[index]=rows;}
function arrival(ch,title,text){const c=C.find(c=>c.id===ch);if(!c.arrival)c.arrival=[];c.arrival.push([title,text]);}
arrival('c1','How to follow this guide','Each objective contains smaller navigation checkpoints. They begin expanded; collapse a section when you have finished reading it. Directions describe the field screen, so “north” means toward the top of the screen unless explicitly labeled world map. Use your version’s Assist control to reveal exits and ladders.');
detail('c1',0,[['Station platform','Before going through the station exit, interact with the fallen guards to receive the opening Potions. The first forced battle is against two MPs; normal attacks are enough. Follow the others through the large gate after the fight.'],['Name the party','Speak with the AVALANCHE members at the reactor entrance. Confirm Cloud’s name, then Barret’s. Follow the group inside; Barret becomes a controllable party member as you approach the interior. There is no benefit to buying or grinding anything before this first dungeon.']]);
detail('c1',1,[['Security doors and side chest','Speak to Biggs to open the first door and Jessie for the next. Before taking the elevator, inspect the small side room for a Phoenix Down. Return to Jessie, enter the lift and operate the wall panel.'],['Catwalks and ladders','After the elevator, descend the stairs and follow Jessie onto the maintenance route. Interact at the ladder to climb down, collect the visible Potion, and continue down toward the circular save point. Save before the last ladder. Random battles begin once you are inside the reactor.']]);
detail('c1',2,[['Pick up the green Materia','Walk along the narrow path toward the center. Interact with Restore on the floor before continuing to the bomb-placement prompt. You cannot freely assign Materia until the later tutorial, but this pickup supplies your first Cure magic.'],['Before placing the bomb','Use Potions to top up if ordinary battles left Cloud or Barret low. You are about to fight a boss and immediately begin an escape timer. The timer starts after that boss, not while you are exploring this approach.']]);
detail('c1',3,[['Attack while the tail is lowered','Cloud has Bolt available; use it for efficient damage. Barret can use Attack. Spend a Limit when available rather than hoarding it for another dungeon. Use a Potion before anyone is close to being knocked out.'],['Wait during the tail stance','The original English warning can read as if you should attack the raised tail. Do the opposite: attacking this stance provokes Tail Laser. Use the interval to heal or wait for the tail to lower, then resume damage. Defeating the boss awards Assault Gun for Barret.']]);
detail('c1',4,[['Retrace the descent','Climb back up the ladders you used to reach the core. The ten-minute countdown continues through menus and battles, so avoid reorganizing equipment here. Stop at Jessie, whose foot is trapped on a platform, and speak to her to free her.'],['Open both exit doors','Return to the elevator and ride up. Jessie and Biggs are needed at the security doors; interact with the waiting allies rather than running repeatedly into a closed doorway. Leave the reactor entrance to trigger the escape scene.']]);
detail('c1',5,[['Sector 8 streets','After the explosion, follow the street toward the flower seller. Buying a flower is optional and feeds later affection choices. Pick up the visible Potion as you move through the street. Continue south toward the soldiers; fighting them earns small rewards, but escaping by the story sequence also works.'],['Inside the train','After Cloud boards, talk to Jessie to see the Midgar explanation and talk to Barret to advance. The train delivers you to Sector 7. Once the timer is no longer a concern, equip Barret’s Assault Gun through the Equip menu.']]);
detail('c2',0,[['Station to the hideout','From the train platform, head toward the slum entrance on the left rather than entering the Train Graveyard. The graveyard is optional training at this point. Cross the town square and enter the bar, Seventh Heaven.'],['Conversations and the flower','Talk to Tifa, Marlene and Barret as their scenes become available. If you bought the flower, your gift choice can affect affection. Give it to the character that fits your intended date route; there is no universally correct story choice. Use the pinball machine to reach the basement when the meeting starts.']]);
detail('c2',1,[['Finish the night’s events','Follow the basement conversation, try to leave when prompted, and complete the talk with Tifa. After payment and rest, the next morning introduces the party’s second mission. Talk to Tifa and Barret rather than immediately walking out.'],['Understand linked Materia','When Barret offers the explanation, use it if needed. A colored orb grants an ability or effect only while equipped. Two slots connected by a short line form a linked pair; adjacent slots without the connecting line do not. All must be connected to a compatible magic Materia to work.']]);
detail('c2',2,[['The weapon shop’s upper floor','Enter the weapon shop in the slums and climb to the beginner instruction room. Pick up the blue All Materia on the floor; interact with the nearby treasure for the Ether as well. The tutorial figures explain rows, Limits and saving.'],['Build a basic healer','Put Restore in a linked slot and All in its connected partner. A group Cure consumes one of All’s per-battle uses; the number increases as the Materia earns AP. Put a second healing option on someone else if possible, so one KO does not leave the group helpless.']]);
detail('c2',3,[['Buy defense before extra spell copies','The equipment counter sells Iron Bangles. Keep at least one for a collection, since early shop stock and starting gear can become unavailable. Buy enough healing items to recover without magic, and a few Phoenix Downs. Fire adds a useful damage type if affordable.'],['Use rows deliberately','Barret’s ranged gun can attack from the back row without the usual physical damage penalty. Moving a close-range fighter back cuts incoming physical damage but usually reduces their physical output too. Avoid filling every slot with unnecessary magic just because the slots are empty; magic Materia often reduces maximum HP.']]);
detail('c2',4,[['Save and board','Make a town save, then head right toward the station and board the waiting train. Tifa accompanies Cloud and Barret for the next operation. Check your equipment before boarding, because the security inspection asks you to move quickly.']]);
detail('c3',0,[['Move before each countdown expires','Talk to Tifa once the train sequence begins. When the security alert starts, run to the next carriage immediately. There are optional passengers with small gifts, but only stop if you have time. Reaching the far carriage is more important than a consumable.'],['If a thief bumps Cloud','A passenger can steal from Cloud during the carriage sequence. Catch and speak to him if you want the item back, then continue forward. Missing a carriage deadline changes where you are forced off; it does not make the playthrough unwinnable.']]);
detail('c3',1,[['Tunnel to the ventilation shaft','After the jump, follow the rail tunnel toward the security beams. You cannot simply run through the beam barrier; interact with the maintenance opening to its side and enter the shaft. Descend into the under-plate service area.'],['Follow the maintenance platforms','Use the ladders to reach the lower catwalks. Check the small side paths for the Ether, Potion and Tent before continuing. The ladder routes reconnect; follow the AVALANCHE members toward the reactor interior and use the save point.']]);
detail('c3',2,[['Take the lower core route first','In the familiar reactor interior, descend toward the core instead of heading straight up to the exit lift. At the core, finish Cloud’s scene and the charge placement. Return along the same ladders and platforms.'],['Use the upper exit','Back at the interior stairs, take the route upward to the elevator. This mission does not put a ten-minute escape countdown on your route back. Collect the Ether near the upper exit before moving to the three-switch console.']]);
detail('c3',3,[['Match the switch timing','Stand at Cloud’s switch with Tifa and Barret at the other two. Watch their practice timing and press your Confirm control at the same instant. If the door does not open, repeat; there is no penalty for another attempt.'],['Prepare for the bridge battle','Use the nearby save opportunity and heal all three characters. Give someone other than Cloud a healing option too: the coming fight separates him from the other two around the enemy, so group targeting behaves differently from a normal formation.']]);
detail('c3',4,[['Work around its facing','Air Buster rotates between the two sides. A physical hit to its back is much stronger than a front hit, so attack with the group it is facing away from. Cloud’s Bolt is also effective against the machine.'],['After the explosion','Finish the dialogue while Cloud hangs from the bridge. These responses can affect affection, but neither option changes the next playable location. The story carries Cloud to the Sector 5 church.']]);
detail('c4',0,[['From flower bed to rafters','Talk to Aeris in the church and follow her when Reno and the soldiers arrive. Move to the rear of the church and climb toward the rafters. Cloud and Aeris become separated during the escape.'],['Help from above','When she calls for help, you can make her fight, have her wait for a barrel, or attempt other responses. If aiming for favorable affection through barrels, the useful order is the leftmost barrel, then the topmost, then the rightmost. Errors lead to small fights or affection changes rather than a blocked route. Continue across the beams and rooftops after reuniting.']]);
detail('c4',1,[['Reach the small settlement','Follow Aeris across the rooftops until you return to the street, then enter the Sector 5 shopping area. The house with the sleeping boy has a Turtle’s Paradise notice upstairs. Read the wall notice now so it counts for the later six-flyer reward.'],['Leave the hidden money','Inspect the child’s hidden compartment if you like, but do not take the 5 gil if you want the later, better reward. The shops offer supplies; conserve gil if your existing gear is sufficient for the next few fights.']]);
detail('c4',2,[['Garden pickups','Leave the settlement through the upper-right path to reach the house and flower garden. Walk through the garden before entering: Cover and an Ether are outside. Cover makes its wearer intercept some physical attacks aimed at allies.'],['The house and rest','Enter, meet Elmyra, and follow the conversation. Aeris asks about Tifa; that answer affects affection. Go upstairs and rest when directed, rather than trying to cross Sector 6 before the night scene completes.']]);
detail('c4',3,[['Walk past the bedroom','After waking, collect the nearby supplies and move quietly toward the stairs. Running near Aeris’s door wakes her and sends you back to bed. Hold the walk modifier if your port defaults to running.'],['Rejoin at the exit','Leave the house and head back through the slums toward Sector 6. Aeris catches up as part of the intended sequence. You have not failed an escort objective by meeting her again; continue together.']]);
detail('c4',4,[['Cross the broken roadway','Use the visible planks, collapsed road and narrow debris route to work through Sector 6. Assist markers help identify the screen exits. At the playground, finish the conversation, then follow the carriage toward Wall Market on the right.'],['Before the market','Keep Restore accessible and save when possible. Wall Market is a largely noncombat investigation sequence, but it leads directly into the sewers and the return toward Sector 7.']]);
detail('c5',0,[['Confirm where Tifa went','In Wall Market, visit the Honey Bee Inn entrance and ask the man outside about Tifa. Then go north to Don Corneo’s mansion and talk to the doorman. He admits women, which begins Cloud and Aeris’s disguise plan.'],['Understand the optional contest','A dress and wig are enough to progress. Better disguise pieces increase Cloud’s chance of being chosen by Corneo, but the story route continues even if another character is selected. Keep a separate save if you want to see a particular selection scene.']]);
detail('c5',1,[['Find the dressmaker','Enter the clothing shop and speak to the woman behind the counter. Her father is drinking in the bar. Speak to him there and choose the material and feel for the dress. For a strong result, choose the soft and shimmering preferences.'],['Return for the fitting','Go back to the clothing shop after arranging the dress. Cloud tries it on, then the shopkeeper directs you toward the gym for a wig. You do not obtain the wig merely by asking at the clothing shop.']]);
detail('c5',2,[['Squat timing','At the gym, accept the squat challenge. Follow the three-button sequence displayed by your version and keep a steady rhythm. Pressing too fast makes Cloud pause, so accuracy matters more than frantic input.'],['Reward quality','Winning yields the best wig, a tie a middling one, and losing the poorest version. Every result permits the story to continue. Do not reload a long stretch unless the specific Corneo-selection outcome matters to you.']]);
detail('c5',3,[['Tiara errand','Visit the Materia shop and accept the shopkeeper’s request. Stay at the inn, use its vending machine at night and purchase the most expensive option for the best return. Bring the item back to the shopkeeper for the tiara.'],['Cologne errand','Eat at the restaurant, give the favorable response and receive the pharmacy coupon. Exchange it for Digestive, then give that to the person occupying the bar bathroom. She rewards you with the strongest cologne. Other medicines lead to different rewards.'],['Honey Bee Inn and makeup','Get the member’s card from the man outside the inn after the disguise investigation begins. Inside, choose one of the available event rooms; each produces different underwear and scenes, so one run cannot show every branch. Before leaving, use the dressing-room makeup option if pursuing the best disguise.']]);
detail('c5',4,[['Change, then enter','Return to the clothing shop to put the outfit on. Go to the mansion, proceed downstairs to find Tifa, and finish the basement conversation before the selection upstairs.'],['If Cloud is not selected','Fight through the room where Cloud is sent, then regroup with the others. Check the mansion rooms for supplies before confronting Corneo in the bedroom. If Cloud is selected, the bedroom scene is reached directly. Both outcomes lead to the same sewer transition.']]);
detail('c6',0,[['Recover after the drop','Cloud, Tifa and Aeris land in the sewer. Talk to your companions, heal, and prepare before moving far enough to trigger Aps. Fire and Limit Breaks are useful; its sewer-wave attacks can injure itself as well as your party.'],['Keep the group stable','Do not spend every action on damage. Restore + All helps recover after Sewer Tsunami; use individual Potions if group magic or MP is unavailable. The fight is followed by exploration, so preserve enough resources to reach the next save.']]);
detail('c6',1,[['First sewer chamber','Explore the walkways around the channel before climbing out. Pick up the yellow Steal Materia from the accessible side of the sewer and equip it if you want to begin collecting enemy equipment.'],['Ladders toward the graveyard','Follow the passage into the next sewer area, cross the narrow paths over the water and use the exit ladder. Collect visible consumables on branches before leaving, since this particular sewer route is not a convenient later return trip.']]);
detail('c6',2,[['First graveyard screen','Use train roofs as walkways: climb a ladder, cross a carriage roof and descend on the other side where the ground path is blocked. Inspect the open barrels along the paths for items. Ghosts are a source of Ghost Hand; collect it now for a consumable collection.'],['Optional enemy equipment','Steal can obtain useful equipment in the graveyard, including Aeris’s Striking Staff from Eligor if you encounter it. Do not make the whole party depend on magic while attempting repeated steals; keep a healer or Potions available.'],['Second graveyard screen','Enter each usable locomotive cab and operate it to shift the engine. Moving the first clears access to the other; shifting the second creates a roof crossing. Return to the ladders, climb over the aligned train roofs and leave toward Sector 7.']]);
detail('c6',3,[['At the base of the pillar','Finish the scene with the slum residents and use the save point. Climb the metal stairs, stopping to speak to the injured AVALANCHE members if you want their dialogue. There is no need to race an invisible countdown on this ascent.'],['Prepare Barret at the top','When Barret joins, open the menu before approaching the confrontation. His Materia and equipment may not match your current setup. Heal all three and keep a way to cure or revive on more than one person.']]);
detail('c6',4,[['Remove Pyramid manually','When Reno traps someone, select Attack and target that ally’s pyramid. This removes it; waiting for it to wear off is unsafe. Do not let all three party members remain trapped.'],['Finish the escape','After Reno retreats, inspect the control situation, complete the conversations, and follow the group to the escape wire. The story then takes you back toward the Sector 6 playground and Aeris’s house.']]);
detail('c7',0,[['Backtrack through Sector 6','From the playground, follow the broken roadway back into Sector 5. If you left the sleeping boy’s money earlier, revisit his house for the improved reward. Then take the upper-right garden route to Aeris’s house.'],['Elmyra’s account','Enter the house and finish the conversations about Aeris. Talk to Barret and the others as needed before departing. This is also a chance to heal and buy supplies before the longer rescue mission.']]);
detail('c7',1,[['Buy the Batteries','Return to Wall Market and enter the weapon shop. Talk to the man at the left side to buy the Batteries for the climb. Without these, the powered obstacles above the market cannot all be crossed.'],['Make a rescue-mission save','Stock healing items, Phoenix Downs and status cures. Cloud, Tifa and Barret form the infiltration group. Check that Barret has a ranged weapon and someone can provide group healing; the building ends with a ranged elevator battle and a solo Cloud battle.']]);
detail('c7',2,[['Find the wire','Go north in Wall Market toward the children gathered beside the wall. Follow them to the climbable wire and interact to ascend. This route leads up the plate wreckage; the mansion is not the way to Shinra HQ.'],['Keep following the metal route','At each screen, use the protruding pipes and girders to continue upward. Assist markers reveal the transitions if the pre-rendered background makes a ladder or cable difficult to distinguish.']]);
detail('c7',3,[['Battery sockets','Install Batteries in the machinery that moves a propeller and another obstruction into usable positions. Cross the newly created paths and continue upward. One later battery socket is only an optional Ether reward; collection players can leave that socket unused to retain a Battery.'],['Swinging cable','Stand at the jump point and watch a full swing first. Press Confirm as the cable comes close enough for Cloud to grab, rather than when it is at the far end of its arc. If you miss, try again. Continue up the final ladder route to the Shinra plaza.']]);
detail('c7',4,[['Front entrance: combat and lower-floor exploration','Entering the glass front doors puts you in the lobby and leads to guard fights and the elevator route. You can examine the foyer flyer and second-floor shop on this route. It is generally faster than climbing the entire back stairwell, and yields combat rewards.'],['Rear entrance: long, quiet stair climb','From the plaza, take the route around the left side to the rear stairwell. It is a long series of landings with party banter and a visible Elixir on one landing. This avoids the front-route elevator encounters and brings you to floor 59.'],['Recommended collection approach','Neither entrance locks you out of all lower floors. Choose the route you prefer, but explicitly visit the lobby for Turtle’s Paradise flyer #2 before the rescue is over. If you take the stairs, use the elevators to return to the lower floors after reaching 59. The next chapter explains both routes and the lobby in full.']]);
arrival('c8','Start here: both entrances meet on floor 59','Cloud, Tifa and Barret are the active group. Save outside the building. The front and rear routes are alternatives, not different story branches; you can still use lower-floor elevators during the infiltration. For a collection run, visit the lobby flyer and the rear-stair Elixir rather than assuming your chosen entrance covers everything.');
detail('c8',0,[['Option A · enter through the front','Use the main glass doors from the plaza. Defeat the entrance guards, then explore the ground-floor foyer before taking the elevator. You will encounter more guards on the elevator route, so keep Cure available. This is the direct, combat-oriented approach.'],['The lobby · Turtle’s Paradise flyer #2','On the first floor, examine the wall notice by the elevator area and read Turtle’s Paradise #2. Reading it sets a sidequest flag; nothing appears in your item bag. The building is only revisited once, during the Disc 2 raid, so do this now rather than leaving it to memory.'],['Second-floor shop and the locked chests','Use the lobby stairs to reach the second floor. Enter the shop at the north side, resupply if needed, and inspect the television for the Shinra vehicle commercial. The two chests here cannot be claimed on this initial visit; return for them during the later Midgar raid. Do not waste time searching for a missing shop key.'],['Take the front elevators','Return to the elevator bank and use an available lift. The initial ride can stop for encounters or an employee scene; defeat hostile occupants and continue riding upward. The route eventually deposits the party on floor 59. Ordinary floors below that are not a set of explorable dungeons.'],['Option B · rear stairwell','If you prefer the back route, go around the building’s left exterior to the rear entrance instead of entering the glass doors. Climb every landing while Cloud, Tifa and Barret exchange dialogue. Pick up the visible Elixir on the climb. The stairs emerge on 59; they do not bypass the keycard floors above.'],['Collection route if you chose the stairs','After reaching 59 and dealing with its guards, use an elevator to revisit the first-floor lobby and read the flyer. Check the second-floor shop if you need supplies. Then return to 59. You do not need to repeat the entire stair climb to continue.'],['Floor 59 · earn Keycard 60','Approach the guards blocking access and defeat the Mighty Grunts. Their reward gives access to 60. Heal after the battle, then use the lift to select the next permitted floor. A keycard authorizes a range; you still have to choose the destination at the elevator controls.'],['Floor 60 · statue cover','Enter the room on the left and move between the statues while the patrolling guards are looking away. Stop behind cover before a guard turns. After Cloud crosses, use the displayed signal prompt to bring the other two across one at a time. Getting spotted causes a fight and a retry, rather than permanently failing the rescue.'],['Floor 61 · obtain Keycard 62','Walk around the lounge and talk to the employee who mistakes Cloud for a maintenance worker. Choose the non-revealing response, shown as an ellipsis in the original English dialogue, instead of asking about Aeris. He hands over Keycard 62. Return to the elevator and select 62.']]);
detail('c8',1,[['Meet Mayor Domino','On floor 62, go to the mayor’s office on the left and speak to Domino. He will give a keycard when you identify his password. His assistant Hart sells hints, but you can solve the puzzle without spending gil. The first correct attempt also gives Elemental Materia.'],['Read the library subjects','There are four small library rooms, each assigned a different subject. Read the label outside a room, then inspect both books on each shelf. Find the one title that does not belong with that room’s subject. Do not assume a shelf contains only one readable book.'],['Extract the letters','For each misplaced book, note the number at the beginning of the title. Count that many letters into the title, following the wording your game displays. The four selected letters rearrange into one of Domino’s offered password choices. The solution can vary, so a memorized answer from another run is not reliable.'],['Answer once you have a match','Return to Domino only after you have all four letters and can identify the offered word. Correct on the first guess yields Elemental; later guesses reduce the bonus, but you still receive Keycard 65. If you want the best reward and make a mistake, reload the save from before answering.'],['Equip Elemental thoughtfully','In a weapon, Elemental linked to Fire, Ice or Lightning adds that element to physical attacks. In armor, the same pair grants resistance, then stronger protection at later levels. Slot placement matters: placing the blue orb elsewhere in the equipment does not link it.']]);
detail('c8',2,[['Floor 63 · start the coupon puzzle','Use the computer in the southeast room to activate door access. You may open three security doors. Before exchanging anything, a bad route can be reset at the computer; once you trade the coupons, treat the puzzle as finished for this visit. Aim to collect all three before exchanging.'],['Floor 63 · first two doors and A Coupon','From the computer room, follow the outer corridor north along the right wall, then go west along the top. Open the first blocking door. Continue west and open the left of the two doors leading downward. Enter the far-west room to collect A Coupon.'],['Floor 63 · vents, B Coupon and C Coupon','In A’s room, enter the air duct. Follow the branch to the room to the right containing B Coupon, rather than returning all the way to the computer room. Leave B’s room and use your final door opening to enter the adjoining middle room for C Coupon. Return through the vent to the computer room.'],['Floor 63 · exchange the set','Exchange A, B and C together for Star Pendant, Four Slots and All. Star Pendant protects from poison; Four Slots offers four independent Materia slots, while All is especially valuable for another group-spell pairing. If you cannot reach all three, reset before trading any coupon and redo the route.'],['Floor 64 · heal, save, check lockers','This recreation floor contains beds and a save point. Rest to restore HP and MP, then save in a separate slot. Search the locker room for its Ether and Phoenix Down. The megaphone that Cloud says is too large is not obtainable yet; it becomes Cait Sith’s HP Shout on the Disc 2 visit.'],['Floor 65 · repair the Midgar model','Open the initially available chest to obtain a model piece. Examine an incomplete section of the large Midgar model and insert it. This unlocks another chest elsewhere on the floor. Repeat the chest → model cycle until all available model sections are repaired.'],['Floor 65 · final keycard','After the model pieces are used, the remaining chest by the stairway contains Keycard 66. Collect it before leaving. The blank central portion is not an extra piece you need to find; do not keep searching for a seventh plate section. Enemies begin appearing on these upper floors, so heal before climbing.']]);
detail('c8',3,[['Floor 66 · bathroom entrance','Go to the restroom in the northwest part of the floor and enter the stall. Use the option to climb onto the toilet, then enter the ventilation duct. Crawl to the end and observe the board meeting. Once the scene finishes, return through the duct and leave the restroom.'],['Follow Hojo to floor 67','Exit toward the stairs and follow the scientist’s route up. On 67, explore the specimen-storage area and collect Poison from its chest. Continue west toward Hojo and the large tank, then follow the laboratory sequence upward. Save and heal before the confrontation.'],['Sample:H0512 · ignore the bait','When Red XIII becomes available, choose the third battle participant and send the other companion to help Aeris. Focus damage on the main Sample:H0512 rather than repeatedly clearing its renewable smaller minions. Magic or a ranged attacker helps reach the rear enemy. Avoid Poison damage here.'],['Floor 68 · collect Enemy Skill','After the fight, walk into the specimen enclosure where the group was held and pick up the yellow Enemy Skill Materia. It is a field pickup, not an automatic battle reward. Speak with the assistant along the walkway for Keycard 68 and check the nearby Potions before returning toward the elevator.'],['Red XIII and the party menu','Red XIII joins during this rescue; no separate optional puzzle is needed to unlock him. Recheck his equipment and remove useful Materia from anyone no longer active. Use the elevators to continue the story; the Turks intercept the group as intended.']]);
detail('c8',4,[['Inside the cells','Follow the president’s scene and the cell conversations. Examine the cell door, speak with Tifa, talk to Aeris through the partition, and check on the other party members as the available prompts change. Rest when the game offers the option. No hidden key needs to be found while the cell is still locked.'],['Follow the trail upward','After Cloud wakes, examine the open door and the fallen guard. Free the others and return to the laboratory. Follow the visible trail through the upper floors to the president’s office, collecting the available key access from the scene rather than trying to leave the building immediately.'],['Floor 69 · split the equipment','Save and heal before the roof confrontation. Cloud will soon fight alone; Barret, Aeris and Red XIII handle the elevator encounters. Give Cloud Restore or enough healing items. Give the elevator group Lightning and its own healer, and use Barret’s ranged gun.'],['Hundred Gunner and Heli Gunner','The elevator enemies are out of normal melee reach. Barret’s gun, offensive magic and usable Limits provide damage; have Aeris or Red XIII support healing. Lightning is effective. After Hundred Gunner falls, Heli Gunner follows, so do not exhaust every resource on the first machine.'],['Cloud versus Rufus','On the roof, defeat Dark Nation first so it stops supporting Rufus. Heal Cloud as needed and use regular attacks and Limits against Rufus. Do not rely on a group-healing pair that was left on the elevator team. After the battle, leave the roof to rejoin Tifa.']]);
detail('c8',5,[['Regroup before the road','Follow Tifa back toward the entrance and complete the vehicle escape scene. When the menu becomes available, redistribute the Materia from the split battles to the three characters who will fight on the highway. Restore everyone’s HP before starting the motorcycle section.'],['Motorcycle controls','Use your version’s left and right attack controls to strike riders approaching the truck. Stay near threatened sides instead of chasing every enemy away from the vehicle. Damage suffered during this sequence affects the condition of the ensuing fight, so protecting the group matters more than a high attack count.'],['Motor Ball','After the chase, face the machine with Lightning and group healing. Recover from its opening and fire attacks before continuing damage. Since the fight changes formation and facing, check rows if physical attacks or incoming hits behave unexpectedly.'],['Final Midgar checklist','Before leaving the city, the key goals were the lobby flyer, Elemental password reward, floor-63 coupons and Enemy Skill pickup. Some missed building pickups have one late return opportunity, but it is safer to record them now. Outside Midgar, choose your three-person group and save on the world map before walking northeast toward Kalm.']]);
SOURCES.push(['Shinra HQ entry and floor reference','Independent cross-check of lobby, shop and floor routes','https://www.arrpeegeez.com/2014/08/final-fantasy-vii-walkthrough-part-six.html'],['Shinra field mechanics','Floor access, coupon rewards and return-visit items','https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Shinra_Bldg._(Final_Fantasy_VII_field)'],['Floor 63 puzzle reference','Coupon route cross-check','https://ff7.info/shinra-building-floor-63.htm'],['Shinra infiltration reference','Additional entry-route and upper-floor cross-check','https://ffextreme.com/ff7/walkthrough1-p10/']);
arrival('c9','World-map preparation','On the world map, open the menu to save almost anywhere you can stand. Kalm is northeast of Midgar. Before crossing the marsh, use Chocobo Lure rather than trying to win a normal fight against the enormous snake.');
detail('c9',0,[['Find the inn','Enter Kalm and go upstairs in the inn. Speak with the group to start Cloud’s account of Nibelheim. The flashback is guided: follow Sephiroth through town, the mountain route and the reactor, then return to the mansion and the town scenes as they unlock.'],['Set the piano flag during the flashback','When free to explore Nibelheim, enter Tifa’s house and inspect the piano in her upstairs room. Confirm that Cloud played it. This is the setup for an extra Elemental Materia during Tifa’s leadership on Disc 2; playing the later Final Heaven melody is a different reward.'],['Explore Kalm afterward','Finish the entire account before leaving the inn. Check cupboards and upstairs rooms around town; repeatedly reach for the item on the inn’s upper cabinet for a Megalixir. The locked chest in one house is not solved during this visit. Visit the weapon and Materia shops before returning to the world map.']]);
detail('c9',1,[['Assign combat roles','A useful early setup is one group healer, one physical attacker, and one caster carrying the enemy’s relevant element. Keep Enemy Skill equipped on someone sturdy if you want to learn Matra Magic from Custom Sweepers around Midgar.'],['Buy what changes the route','Earth, Heal and better weapons are useful purchases in Kalm, but do not spend all your gil before the farm. You still need Chocobo Lure and greens to cross the swamp normally. Carry healing items because repeated random battles can empty the healer’s MP.']]);
detail('c9',2,[['The pen dance','At the farm southeast of Kalm, interact with the Chocobo at the fence and choose the greeting that starts the dance. Watch it finish to receive Choco/Mog. This summon is not purchased from Billy’s shop.'],['Buy the catching tools','Enter the barn, speak to Choco Billy, buy Chocobo Lure and a supply of greens, then equip the purple Materia. At this point you catch a temporary riding Chocobo; the breeding stables do not open until the Highwind phase.']]);
detail('c9',3,[['Use the tracks','Walk on the Chocobo footprints outside the farm with the lure equipped. A successful encounter includes a Chocobo alongside ordinary enemies. Feed it greens to keep it occupied, then defeat the other enemies without hitting the bird. If it runs, try another encounter.'],['Cross the marsh while mounted','After the battle, mount the Chocobo and head across the swamp toward the cave on the far side. Keep moving while the Midgar Zolom is away from your path. Dismounting abandons this temporary ride, so wait until you have crossed safely. The impaled-snake scene on the far side marks the story route.']]);
detail('c9',4,[['Mine treasure branch','Inside Mythril Mine, explore the right-hand side before taking the main exit route. Use the climbable vine to the elevated ledge for Long Range. Check the nearby treasure for the Ether and Tent, and inspect the other upper branches for the Elixir and Mind Source.'],['Follow the Turks to the exit','Return to the connecting tunnel and continue through the scene with the Turks. Exit on the far side to the Junon region. This is the earliest normal opportunity to recruit Yuffie: search the nearby forest before entering Junon if you want her as soon as possible.']]);
arrival('c10','Recruit Yuffie before Junon','With Mythril Mine behind you, the forests in this region can produce Mystery Ninja. Defeat her and follow the Characters section’s exact dialogue sequence. Do this before proceeding to Junon for the earliest possible optional recruitment. Fort Condor also has three separate early defense windows around this part of the route.');
detail('c10',0,[['Optional Fort Condor visit','From the mine exit, visit the large bird-topped fort to the south. Agree to help and climb to the commander for the first defense. The strategy battle costs gil for units; you can skip the optional battle without losing access to the later mandatory Huge Materia mission.'],['Yuffie’s encounter','Walk in the forests near Junon until Mystery Ninja appears. After winning, do not use the apparent save point. Reply: Not interested → …petrified → Wait a second! → …That’s right → …Let’s hurry on. Asking her name at the end lets her escape.'],['Approach lower Junon','Junon is the coastal settlement under the huge cannon, north of the fort. Enter the lower village, check the houses and shops, then take the descending route to the beach where Priscilla and the dolphin are waiting.']]);
detail('c10',1,[['Prepare for an airborne target','Bottomswell is not reachable with ordinary short-range attacks. Give Cloud Long Range or offensive magic, use Barret’s gun or Yuffie’s ranged weapon, and keep a healer separate from your primary caster.'],['Waterpolo bubbles','If an ally is imprisoned in a bubble, direct a damaging spell at the bubble to break it. Do not spend the whole battle targeting the boss while a character is suffocating. Maintain party HP because the fight can end with a final wave attack.']]);
detail('c10',2,[['CPR and rest','After the battle, interact with Priscilla. Fill Cloud’s breathing meter and release a breath, repeating until she recovers. Follow the villagers’ directions to rest in the house. After the night sequence, visit Priscilla again to receive Shiva.'],['Fort Condor’s short windows','For every optional defense, return after Bottomswell but before advancing Priscilla’s recovery, then again after the dolphin introduction but before going to upper Junon. These are separate attacks and easily skipped by following the main story immediately.'],['Use the dolphin','At the beach, use the whistle to have the dolphin launch Cloud. A simple original-game solution is to remain at the starting position and whistle twice without moving between attempts. Once on the beam, climb the ladder, use the platform control and enter the airport buildings.']]);
detail('c10',3,[['Get the uniform','Follow the captain into the locker area, inspect the open locker and change into a Shinra uniform. Practice the marching commands with the soldiers. Outside, watch the line and join the formation from its rear instead of trying to push in from the side.'],['Parade rewards are optional','Match the march and rifle movement to the instructions. A poor television rating only changes the prize; it does not send you back to the lower town or stop the story. Keep going with the soldiers after the performance.']]);
detail('c10',4,[['Inspect the training room','Explore both upper-Junon streets before following the final departure sequence. Enter the beginner training area in the barracks and collect its Enemy Skill Materia. This is the second independent copy: learned skills from the first do not transfer automatically.'],['Shop and preserve early stock','Check the equipment shops for upgrades and, if collecting, buy Mythril Clip before later story progression changes stock. The street contains optional NPC conversations and buildings; do not assume the captain’s route is the only explorable path.'],['Send-off and boarding','At the dock, follow the captain’s rifle commands for Rufus’s send-off. The better rewards include Force Stealer at a high score, but any outcome permits boarding. Enter the cargo ship when the event ends.']]);
detail('c11',0,[['Talk throughout the passenger area','Your companions wear disguises around the ship. Speak to them, then locate Barret watching from the bow/deck area after the initial conversations. A visible blue All Materia near Yuffie can be collected once she moves after the alarm.'],['Before the alarm route','Marines encountered on this ship can be stolen from for Shinra Beta. This armor has a later reactor opportunity too, but the ship is a convenient early source. Do not leave your only healer without MP while chasing steals.']]);
detail('c11',1,[['Re-form the group','After the alarm, speak to the companions and form the three-person battle party. Save at the ship’s save point and heal. Descend toward the cargo hold; inspect the chest on the upper walkway for Wind Slash before approaching the central disturbance.'],['Battle preparation','Equip Restore + All and a summon or strong elemental spell. The next encounter can strike repeatedly, so a second item-based healer is valuable. You are not choosing a special party to unlock a character here.']]);
detail('c11',2,[['Jenova∙BIRTH','Keep the healer ready for repeated Laser and Tail Laser pressure. Use your best current attacks and Limits rather than spending turns on weak effects that do not improve survival. A stunned or knocked-out healer should be supported by items from another party member.'],['Stop before exiting','When the battle ends, walk to the red Materia in the hold and collect Ifrit. It is not awarded in the results screen. Leaving this room without it permanently loses the individual summon; check the Materia menu before using the exit.']]);
detail('c11',3,[['Town and basement','On reaching Costa del Sol, explore the houses and the villa’s accessible basement for its early treasure, including Power Source, Motor Drive and Fire Ring. Buying the villa itself is an optional luxury and unnecessary for story progress.'],['Conversations and supplies','Your inactive party members appear around town with optional dialogue. Visit them before leaving if you want the first-arrival scenes. Check the bar’s equipment vendor for Four Slots while early stock is active, then rest and exit west to the world map.']]);
detail('c11',4,[['Find the mountain trail','From Costa del Sol, follow the land route inland and north toward Mount Corel. Enter the mountain path instead of trying to cross the sea again. Pass the reactor structure and descend toward the long railway screens.'],['Prepare for the railway','The bridges contain random encounters, including Bombs that can supply useful offensive items through Steal. Save on the world map before entering if you want to retry falling-track treasures without replaying the ship.']]);
detail('c12',0,[['Explore railway forks','Follow the rails from the reactor into the broken mountain railway. Take the accessible upper and lower branches for W Machine Gun, Turbo Ether and Transform before leaving the area. Train-track gaps can break beneath Cloud.'],['Falling-track treasure','When Cloud falls, use the left or right directional prompt during the descent to reach a treasure ledge. Different sides hold different rewards. Falling is not a game over, and the missed side can be pursued at another break point; save beforehand if you want to control every result.']]);
detail('c12',1,[['The switch hut','When the path divides and your allies cannot cross, send Cloud along the upper track toward the small control hut. Interact with the switch inside to lower the bridge. Return to the railway and cross the newly opened lower route.'],['Side ledges and the bird nest','Before leaving, explore the optional ledge route near the hut. The nest presents a choice with a fight and consumable reward; leaving it alone is also valid. Continue along the long bridge until you reach North Corel.']]);
detail('c12',2,[['North Corel','Explore the tent settlement and speak to its residents for Barret’s background. Rest or buy supplies if needed, then take the ropeway station at the west side to Gold Saucer. You cannot walk straight into the amusement park from the desert beneath it.'],['Admission and saving','The park entrance accepts gil for a single visit or a lifetime ticket. GP is separate currency used by many park games and the park save point. If you do not have GP, keep a world-map save from before riding the ropeway.']]);
detail('c12',3,[['Wonder Square recruitment','Choose the Wonder Square transport from the central hub. Meet Cait Sith and complete his introduction to recruit him. His starting Manipulate Materia is useful for support Enemy Skills.'],['Optional park stops','The Ghost Hotel has Turtle’s Paradise flyer #3. Speed Square’s early 5,000-point prize is Umbrella; claim it before the Highwind story transition if collecting Aeris’s weapons. These activities are optional before the story pushes onward.'],['Go to Battle Square','After the initial park exploration, enter Battle Square and follow the incident there. The resulting prison sequence is mandatory. Once it begins, you must resolve it before returning to unrestricted park exploration.']]);
detail('c12',4,[['Regroup in the prison','Follow Barret, visit the house where the party gathers, and finish the account of Corel. Speak to Mr. Coates about the boss controlling release. You need to find Dyne before the race arrangement proceeds. The truck and town facilities offer a chance to heal.'],['Find the junkyard route','Leave the prison through the north gate. On the next screen, use the gap along the left fence, continue north, then use the opening on the right to reach the junkyard side. If you enter the repeating desert instead, keep working east/right until you reach the canyon leading into the junkyard.'],['Prepare Barret before the northern exit','Move through the scrapped vehicles to the north. The final screen triggers a solo Barret fight, so give him Restore, good armor and his ranged gun first. Back row reduces incoming physical damage without weakening that gun.'],['Dyne’s last attack','Use Big Shot or your current damaging Limit and heal early. Dyne can act aggressively as his HP falls and may attack once more as the battle ends. Keep enough HP for another hit instead of finishing from near zero.']]);
detail('c12',5,[['Return for the race','After Dyne’s sequence, speak to Mr. Coates to complete the race arrangement. Ester takes Cloud to the jockey room. Before speaking to her to start, collect the red Ramuh Materia in the room; you will not have a normal return opportunity.'],['Race with controlled stamina','Use manual control if comfortable. Keep a sustainable pace through most of the course and save the strongest sprint for the late stretch. Holding the shoulder controls that correspond to the original L1 + R1 can help stamina recovery in the original control scheme; remapped ports may differ.'],['After the win','Accept the buggy and read the departure scenes. On the world map it crosses shallow rivers and desert. For the earliest optional returns, drive it into Costa del Sol and use the boat to take it back to the eastern continent, rather than leaving the vehicle outside town.']]);
arrival('c13','A collection route before Cosmo Canyon','Gongaga is optional, but its early events have a deadline. If you want every playable Fort Condor defense, park the buggy away from Cosmo Canyon’s breakdown trigger and enter the canyon on foot; otherwise the vehicle can strand you during one defense window.');
detail('c13',0,[['Locate the forest village','From the Gold Saucer region, drive south toward the circular forest containing a destroyed reactor. Enter Gongaga from the world map and follow the path until Reno and Rude confront you.'],['The paired Turks fight','Focus one opponent to end the encounter more quickly; the other withdraws when his partner falls. Keep group healing ready and use strong attacks rather than spreading damage evenly. The encounter is part of this optional early Gongaga visit.']]);
detail('c13',1,[['Reactor and Titan','At the path junction, explore the reactor branch and watch the Shinra scene. After the visitors leave, inspect the ruined reactor debris to uncover Titan. It is not a reward from defeating Reno and Rude.'],['Village route and personal scenes','Return to the junction and take the village branch. Visit the shops and the house connected to Zack’s parents. Bring Aeris and Tifa for their relevant dialogue and speak to them after they step outside. Finish these early scenes before advancing through the Keystone visit at Gold Saucer.']]);
detail('c13',2,[['Drive west across the river','Return to the world map and cross the shallow river section toward the canyon. If following every Condor defense, leave the buggy well short of Cosmo Canyon and enter on foot. For an ordinary story run, driving up to town triggers a repair-related stop.'],['Enter with Red XIII','At the gate, Red XIII is recognized and leads the party inside. Explore the town’s stairways, inn and equipment shops. Read the Turtle’s Paradise notices in the weapon shop and inn for flyers #4 and #5.']]);
detail('c13',3,[['The observatory route','Follow the vertical stairways and ladders to Bugenhagen’s home at the top. Speak with him, gather the required companions and return for the planetarium demonstration. The town’s stacked screens are connected by obvious ladders once Assist markers are on.'],['Campfire and party choice','After the demonstration, return to the campfire and speak to the companions, finishing with Red XIII. Form the cave party and follow Bugenhagen toward the sealed door. If doing the short-window Condor defense, this is the point to leave and return before descending into the Cave of the Gi.']]);
detail('c13',4,[['Open the first cave gate','In the first chamber, inspect the small side caverns to find the stone that opens the way onward; other stones can produce fights. Collect the consumable treasure along the accessible side paths before advancing.'],['Oil floor and Added Effect','On the slick section, walk rather than run to avoid sliding into spikes. Take the connected lower side route to Added Effect and return to the main passage. The Materia is a permanent one-visit pickup here.'],['Spider-web passages','In the later tunnel, a web blocks some routes and touching it triggers a Stinger fight. Heal between them, since their strong attacks can punish a weakened character. Follow the main upper path through the webs to the final chamber, checking side chests before approaching the boss.']]);
detail('c13',5,[['Use the undead weakness','Gi Nattak is undead, so healing items harm it. An X-Potion is a reliable shortcut against the main body; a Phoenix Down is a chance-based option. Otherwise use normal damage while keeping the party healed and avoiding Fire-based attacks.'],['Collect Gravity and finish the scene','Pick up the Gravity Materia after the battle and continue out to the final story overlook. Red XIII receives Seraph Comb through the events. Return through town and recover the buggy if it was repaired; the Cave of the Gi is not a later cleanup dungeon.']]);
arrival('c14','Recruit Vincent on this visit','You do not need to wait for a later disc. Before crossing Mount Nibel, open the mansion safe, defeat Lost Number, and use its key in the basement. The Characters page has the complete dialogue sequence and the exact safe directions.');
detail('c14',0,[['Town exploration','Enter the houses and speak to the residents to see how this Nibelheim differs from Cloud’s account. Tifa’s house and piano are explorable, but the late Limit reward is not obtained by a first-visit piano attempt. Explore Shinra Mansion at the north end afterward.'],['Mansion side rooms','Check both ground-floor wings and the upstairs rooms for weapons and sources, including Twin Viper, Silver M-phone and Enemy Launcher. Read the letter with safe clues in the left-side room; the invisible fourth clue is selected below the visible entries. You can use the known combination without collecting every clue.']]);
detail('c14',1,[['Find the secret stairway','On the upper floor’s right wing, enter the bedroom with the curved wall opening. Walk through the hidden side passage and descend the spiral stairway to the basement caves. Continue to the library at the far end.'],['Library encounter and Destruct','Approach the rear of the library to trigger the scene. Afterward, pick up Destruct where it lands before leaving. The locked door off the basement corridor is Vincent’s room; its key is obtained from the upstairs safe, not from the library encounter.']]);
detail('c14',2,[['Safe solution','Save outside the mansion first. At the upstairs west-wing safe, turn right to 36, left to 10, right to 59, then right to 97, confirming each number without passing it. You have a short timer. Opening it immediately starts Lost Number, so prepare before dialing.'],['Lost Number and the key','Use a reliable healer and defensive equipment. Near half HP, the boss specializes according to the damage that crosses its transformation threshold. Defeat it, collect Cosmo Memory, then take Odin and the basement key from the safe area.'],['Wake and recruit Vincent','Unlock the coffin room beside the basement corridor. Speak about Sephiroth, then continue talking and ask who he is. When he repeats that he wants to sleep, leave toward the stairs. He catches up and joins. If you have the key but he has not joined, return and finish both dialogue topics.']]);
detail('c14',3,[['Mountain approach and side peaks','Leave town north toward Mount Nibel. Follow the narrow mountain path and rope bridge. Explore the branch climbs for Rune Blade and Plus Barrette before entering the reactor-side caves. These weapons reward exploration, especially their Materia-growth properties.'],['Pipe room navigation','The pipe entrances drop Cloud to different lower ledges. Before testing them, descend by the available route and lower the ladder so you can return to the top. Use the pipes to reach the side treasure, including Powersoul and an All Materia, rather than taking only the direct boss exit.'],['Optional reactor route','The connecting caves also lead toward the old reactor and its surrounding paths. Explore the accessible loops before leaving. Return to the large cave with the save point and Materia Keeper when you are ready to exit toward Rocket Town.']]);
detail('c14',4,[['Prepare the Enemy Skill learner','Equip Enemy Skill before fighting Materia Keeper. Trine is a lightning-based party attack; keep the learner alive through the cast. Do not stack another Enemy Skill copy that already knows Trine on the same character as one that is trying to learn it.'],['Avoid Fire and finish the boss','Materia Keeper absorbs Fire, so use other magic, summons and physical damage. Heal after its stronger moves and use Limits when safe. After victory, collect Counter Attack on the field. It triggers independently and does not need to be connected to another Materia.'],['Exit to Rocket Town','Leave through the lower passage beyond the boss area to return to the world map. Head toward Rocket Town on the far side of the mountain range. Save before entering if you want a clean pre-town record.']]);
detail('c15',0,[['The old man’s weapon','Near the shops, talk repeatedly to the man watching the rocket. When invited, look at it with him and accept Yoshiyuki. Claim it on this visit; its availability is not guaranteed for the whole game.'],['Weapon and item shops','Inspect the current weapon list, including Shotgun for Vincent if collecting. Buy it even if he is not active, because the stock changes after the Highwind transition. Keep enough gil for healing and the optional Tiny Bronco side trips rather than buying every upgrade automatically.']]);
detail('c15',1,[['Cid’s home and the airstrip','Enter the house connected to the Tiny Bronco’s backyard and speak with Shera. Inspect the airstrip to learn who owns the plane. Follow the town route to the leaning rocket and climb its exterior to meet Cid inside.'],['Complete the conversations','After meeting Cid, return to the house for the Shinra visit and Shera’s account. For all Condor defenses, the window after speaking to Shera but before meeting the captain must be handled before you advance these scenes. Otherwise proceed normally toward the backyard confrontation.']]);
detail('c15',2,[['Prepare at the backyard','Before approaching Palmer, equip Cloud’s group and restore HP. Cid’s introduction does not mean you can ignore the party’s existing equipment; he becomes available through the escape afterward.'],['Palmer’s attacks','Mako Gun uses elemental magic. Restore + All keeps the group steady, while physical attacks and Limits provide simple damage. If using Elemental in armor, make sure it is actually linked to the relevant elemental Materia. Finish the fight and follow the escape sequence.']]);
detail('c15',3,[['Tiny Bronco controls','After the landing, the damaged plane travels across light-colored shallow water, not the dark deep ocean. Sail along coastlines and use the shallow channels between continents. Disembark only at a usable shoreline.'],['Cid joins now','Reorganize the party to equip Cid if you want to use him. This is the earliest story recruitment for the ninth character when both optional companions have already been recruited. His starting equipment should be checked like everyone else’s.']]);
detail('c15',4,[['Story route to the Keystone','The next required objective is Dio’s Keystone at Gold Saucer. Travel by shallow water toward the western continent, reach North Corel and take the ropeway. The weaponsmith’s house near Gongaga explains the lead if you want the in-game clue.'],['Optional Wutai and Great Gospel','The Tiny Bronco makes Wutai’s western continent accessible. Complete its Materia-theft rescue before Disc 3 if desired. This phase also opens the Mythril exchange for Great Gospel; finish Aeris’s personal Limit goals before completing the Temple of the Ancients. See the item/event register for both timing warnings.']]);
detail('c16',0,[['Weaponsmith’s lead','Visit the small isolated weaponsmith’s house near Gongaga if you want the story clue. He explains that the Keystone was sold to Dio. If you have Mythril, this is also the exchange that offers Great Gospel from the small upstairs box.'],['Return to North Corel','Use the Tiny Bronco’s shallow-water route to reach the western coast, then travel to North Corel and take the ropeway. Save before entering Gold Saucer if you want a preserved pre-date state. Do any remaining early Gongaga scenes before this progression.']]);
detail('c16',1,[['Inspect the showroom','From the park hub, go to Battle Square and enter Dio’s display room. Examine the Keystone. Agree to his request to try the Battle Arena. Cloud fights alone, so equip his own healing and defense first.'],['You do not need eight wins','Surviving more rounds can earn extra rewards, but Dio hands over the Keystone for participating. Do not reset a long play session merely because the arena run ends early. Afterward, try to leave the park via the ropeway to trigger the overnight stay.']]);
detail('c16',2,[['Hotel meeting','When the ropeway is unavailable, follow the group to the Ghost Hotel. Complete the party discussion and the room sequence. Read flyer #3 here if you have not already.'],['The date','Your companion is chosen from hidden affection values built by earlier decisions. Follow the stage-play prompts and the gondola scene. This guide records the event but does not claim to optimize every platform’s Barret-date achievement; use the separate source guide if a specific trophy is your goal.']]);
detail('c16',3,[['Follow the chase','After the date, Cait Sith leaves with the Keystone. Follow him through the park’s transport hub and successive squares until the dock sequence resolves. Stay with the visible chase rather than starting unrelated park minigames.'],['Return to the group','Finish the confrontation and return to the Ghost Hotel. Speak with the party the following morning, then leave by the repaired ropeway. The next story destination is the southern temple.']]);
detail('c16',4,[['Find the temple island','Return to the Tiny Bronco and follow the shallow-water coastline south of the eastern continent to the temple area. Disembark and enter the forested temple site. Aeris is required for the dungeon, so equip her before progressing.'],['Prepare a permanent pre-temple save','Bring restoration, revival and status cures, and make a separate save outside. Finish Great Gospel use or any other Aeris-specific goals now. Princess Guard, Morph, Luck Plus and Bahamut are inside and must be collected before the temple’s ending.']]);
arrival('c17','Treat this as a one-way treasure dungeon','Save outside before entering. Aeris is required. Do not rush the maze or the clock rooms: several rewards are unique to this visit, and the dungeon cannot be reopened afterward. The clock’s side rooms are optional, but their items are not all replaceable.');
detail('c17',0,[['Entrance and the keystone altar','Climb the outside steps, speak with the injured visitor at the entrance and follow Aeris into the temple. Inspect the altar to use the Keystone and descend. The first interior screen is an isometric maze with stairs, doorways and climbable vines.'],['Use height as well as direction','Follow the Cetra spirit when it moves, but inspect each reachable side platform before taking the next main doorway. Some apparent dead ends contain climbable vines. Use Assist to identify doorway transitions instead of interpreting every decorative wall opening as an exit.'],['Maze pickups before the next corridor','Explore the stepped side routes for Trident, Silver Rifle, Rocket Punch and consumables, and the separate upper route for Luck Plus. The small spirit’s room offers a chance to buy supplies, recover and save. Return to it before long stretches if you need healing.']]);
detail('c17',1,[['Read the curved stones','The rolling obstacles have open, U-shaped gaps. Match Cloud’s position to the opening as a stone passes, then move to the next safe section. Trying to outrun a whole series is less reliable than crossing one gap at a time. Being knocked back means retrying the passage.'],['Do not leave Morph behind','Collect the yellow Morph Materia in this corridor. If the rolling sequence makes it inconvenient to pick up, complete the corridor and return once the stone event has settled. Morph turns some enemies into items when its reduced-damage finishing hit defeats them.'],['Pool and recovery spirit','At the far end, examine the pool and finish the vision. Speak with the spirit for recovery and saving. Continue to the clock chamber only after checking Morph and any remaining corridor treasure.']]);
detail('c17',2,[['Set a bridge with the hands','In the clock room, stop or move the hands using the displayed controls until they join the central disk with the numbered doorway you want. Walk along the stationary hands. The moving second hand can knock you down; this leads to a lower encounter and Nail Bat treasure rather than an immediate game over.'],['Clock side-room sweep','Visit room IV for Princess Guard and room V for Ribbon before committing to the story route. Room VII has Trumpet Shell and VIII a Megalixir. Some other numbered doors are empty or contain battles; inspect them if you want the complete dungeon experience, healing between encounters.'],['Important exit order','The main interior route is VI, where the door keeper puzzle leads onward. XII is the later way back out. Do not assume XII is a shortcut for skipping the temple’s inner scenes, and do not leave unique side-room equipment for a return after the ending.']]);
detail('c17',3,[['How the doorway chase works','The spirit enters one doorway and emerges from a different doorway in the multi-level room. Simply following behind it repeats the chase. Watch where a particular entrance exits, then use the stairs or drop points to get ahead and intercept that exit.'],['Intercept rather than follow','Stand at an exit you have observed it use and let its next route bring it to you. You can repeat attempts without consuming a limited item. Once caught, the spirit opens the locked inner room and provides recovery/save access. Check the Work Glove chest in this section before going through.'],['Red Dragon preparation','In the mural chamber, follow the story and prepare for Red Dragon. Fire protection helps; avoid relying on Fire damage against a fire-themed boss. Use strong physical attacks, Limits and non-fire summons while maintaining healing.']]);
detail('c17',4,[['Pick up Bahamut on the field','After Red Dragon, collect the red Bahamut Materia from the chamber before doing anything that leaves it behind. Equip it if you want a powerful non-elemental option for the following boss. It does not automatically enter the collection after the fight.'],['Inspect the model','Examine the temple model/Black Materia device, finish the conversations and follow Cait Sith’s plan. Retrace the inner route to the clock room. Before using XII, verify Princess Guard, Ribbon, Morph and Luck Plus in your inventory if those are your collection goals.']]);
detail('c17',5,[['Final save and equipment','Use the spirit’s recovery and save before the exit-side encounter. Give your healer Restore + All; Barrier can soften physical pressure and Time helps establish Haste. Equip Ribbon or carry Soft for petrification-related problems.'],['Demons Gate strategy','This boss’s high magic defense makes ordinary spells less impressive than good physical damage, Limits and Bahamut. Keep the party ready for Demon Rush when it moves forward. A healer’s prepared action is more valuable than squeezing in a weak attack before that rush.'],['After the temple','Finish the long story sequence without assuming another shopping or training stop is coming inside the dungeon. When control returns elsewhere, the party’s available roster changes. Continue the northern lead through Bone Village, keeping the separate pre-temple save if you want to revisit Aeris’s training.']]);
detail('c18',0,[['Sail north','Use the Tiny Bronco to follow shallow coastal water to the northern continent. Bone Village is the excavation camp on the southern approach to the forest. Enter and speak to the foreman near the lower tents.'],['Buy supplies before digging','The camp sells equipment and supplies appropriate for the next stretch. Heal on the world map if needed. The immediate key item is Lunar Harp; generic excavation rewards do not open the forest.']]);
detail('c18',1,[['Start a Lunar Harp excavation','Ask to search for the Lunar Harp. You may hire workers and place them on the field; after triggering the search, they face toward the treasure. The target is on the upper level around the tent area, rather than in the lower entrance field.'],['Use intersecting sight lines','Place workers on different sides of the upper area, set off the search and compare their facing directions. Mark the spot near the intersection and finish the day. Check the result in the morning. A bad dig costs another attempt, not the key item forever.']]);
detail('c18',2,[['Wake the Sleeping Forest','With Lunar Harp in Key Items, enter the forest at the back of the camp. The first transition activates the forest; you do not equip the harp as Materia or manually use it from the ordinary Item list.'],['Catch the wandering summon','In the forest screen, a small red Materia moves among the trees. Wait for it to approach a reachable position and interact to collect Kjata. Continue north after collecting it instead of mistaking the wandering glow for background decoration.']]);
detail('c18',3,[['Valley treasure','Follow the path beyond the forest through the rock and shell formations. Take the visible side branch to Water Ring before entering the capital. This accessory is particularly useful against the coming water-based boss.'],['Explore all three city branches','At the capital’s entrance, the paths fan left, center and right. Explore the left-side buildings for treasure, then the right-hand houses for Guard Source and the resting house. Inspect the upper rooms and chests rather than immediately taking the central route.'],['Do not rest too early if tracking Condor','Awakening the forest opens one Fort Condor window; sleeping in the capital opens another. If checking every defense, complete the first trip before resting. Otherwise rest in the right-side house to unlock the next story route.']]);
detail('c18',4,[['The third Enemy Skill','In the house with beds, inspect the area behind the beds for the yellow Enemy Skill Materia. It is easy to miss because the beds obscure it. This copy begins with its own empty skill list.'],['Return to the center after resting','After the overnight scene, go back to the central path. The way inside the central structure now leads down to the underground passage. Collect Comet on the upper/interior route before descending farther, then save before the altar.']]);
detail('c18',5,[['Altar and boss transition','Follow the stepping stones toward the altar and complete the scripted inputs and scene. A boss battle follows, so enter with your party healed rather than using the approach as a last chance to reorganize afterward.'],['Jenova∙LIFE and the Water Ring','Equip Water Ring on a reliable survivor so its water absorption provides a safe recovery anchor. Heal or revive the others as needed and deal steady damage. Finish the scenes before heading back out of the capital.'],['Northern exit','The next route leaves the capital to the northeast and follows the spiral shell and mountain trail toward Icicle Inn. This begins the original Disc 2 story division even on digital versions with no physical disc change.']]);
SOURCES.push(['Corel Prison route','Junkyard access and the solo battle cross-check','https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/ps/197341-final-fantasy-vii/faqs/71240/corel-prison'],['Great Glacier field reference','Landmark-based navigation and snowboard landing points','https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Great_Glacier_(Final_Fantasy_VII_field)'],['Original official guide','Your BradyGames reference · David Cassady, 1997','https://archive.org/details/final-fantasy-7-official-strategy-guide']);
arrival('c19','Choose a consistent glacier starting point','The snowboard forks change your landing point. For the route described below, take LEFT at the first fork and LEFT at the second to land in the forest. The glacier uses connected landmark screens; different guides number those screens differently, so this guide names the landmarks instead.');
detail('c19',0,[['The shell ascent','Leave the capital by the northeast route. Climb the large spiral shell from its lower path to the top and enter the adjoining cave. Walk around the shell’s side for Viper Halberd before committing upward.'],['Cracks, ledges and ladder treasure','In the mountain passage, climb the visible wall cracks to move between ledges. Inspect the side chests for Bolt Armlet and HypnoCrown. Near the last ladder, descend to the lower branch for Magic Plus before climbing out to the snowy world map. Travel west and then north toward Icicle Inn.']]);
detail('c19',1,[['Explore before leaving downhill','Visit the weapon shop and the houses. In the house with the glacier map, examine the map on the wall and take it. In Gast’s house, inspect the video machine and play the recordings if you want the optional background scenes; the map is in another building.'],['Elena and the snowboard','Trying the northern exit triggers Elena’s confrontation. Follow the scene, then visit the injured child’s house to obtain the snowboard. Once it is in Key Items, return to the northern slope and agree to descend. You cannot walk the entire route in place of this initial snowboard trip.']]);
detail('c19',2,[['Control your landing','For a repeatable starting point, choose left at both course splits. This lands in the glacier forest, where a Mind Source lies behind a tree near the top. The course score is not a requirement for continuing the main story.'],['Other fork outcomes','Left then right lands at the Ice Gate, right then right at the cavern entrance, and right then left near the lone-tree area. If you land somewhere else, use the map’s shapes and exits to identify the landmark rather than restarting just to match a guide’s screen number.']]);
detail('c19',3,[['Forest to lake and crossroads','From the forest, head right/east to the frozen lake. The lake’s lower-right exit leads toward the eastern cave entrance; go north from that entrance area to reach the crossroads. The lake also has a side ice-floe puzzle leading to Safety Bit, so explore that branch before continuing if collecting accessories.'],['Reach and touch the hot spring','From the crossroads, take a northbound route to the hot spring landmark. On arrival, interact at the water’s edge and choose to touch it. Merely passing through the spring screen does not set the condition for Snow’s Alexander battle. The downward connecting snow path also contains Added Cut; inspect the small colored pickup against the white ground.'],['Alexander route from the cabin','After touching the water, a reliable reset point is Holzoff’s cabin, reached by continuing north or by cold exhaustion. Leave the cabin south into the marker snowfield. Travel toward the central cave for All, then exit the cave and head east/right across the snowfield to the eastern cave network. Continue through the connecting snow, ice and rock screens to Snow’s cave.'],['Snow’s battle','Speak to the woman in the cave after touching the spring. Defeat Snow, then collect Alexander from the field. Without the hot-spring flag she does not produce the same encounter. The glacier can be revisited later, so a missed Alexander is not the same kind of permanent loss as Neo Bahamut in the next one-way area.']]);
detail('c19',4,[['Keep a direction in the whiteout','The large snowfield periodically rotates the view during a gust. Place a line of markers while walking so you can realign with your previous heading after the rotation. Turn back toward that line instead of continuing along the screen’s new apparent north.'],['Cold exhaustion is recoverable','After prolonged exposure, Cloud collapses and wakes in Holzoff’s cabin. This is a navigation reset, not a game over. Leave south to explore unfinished glacier landmarks, or go north from the cabin to begin Gaea’s Cliff after resting and saving.']]);
detail('c19',5,[['Use the cabin as a base','Talk to Holzoff, rest, and save in a separate slot. Check that you have protection or cures for petrification and other statuses. Malboros later in this route can inflict several effects at once, making Ribbon valuable.'],['One-way boundary','The Great Glacier itself can be revisited; the Gaea’s Cliff climb beyond the cabin cannot be freely repeated after the crater sequence. Finish its Ribbon, Javelin and Enemy Skill opportunities on this trip.']]);
detail('c20',0,[['Warm up at every ledge','Outside the caves, climb to a ledge and repeatedly use the displayed warming control before taking the next wall route. Keep your temperature well above the danger range. Falling unconscious sends you back down rather than revealing an alternate route upward.'],['Follow the marked climb points','At junctions, use the climb prompts and small flags rather than trying to scale every visible surface. The first ascent brings you into the lower ice cave; explore there before taking another exterior climb.']]);
detail('c20',1,[['Ribbon behind the hidden wall','In the first cave, search the wall along the upper passage for the concealed side entrance. Walk through into the hidden room and open the Ribbon chest. Because the opening blends into the ice background, do not assume a solid-looking wall means that the corridor ends.'],['Javelin and the boulder','Return to the upper path and take the chest on its right side for Javelin. Continue through the connecting cave to the large boulder and push it. It breaks an obstruction below, opening the route that was previously impassable. Return to that lower path and proceed through the new opening.']]);
detail('c20',2,[['Fight the icicles individually','In the upper cave, the hanging icicles are battle targets. Defeat them so they fall to the floor below. After each fight, choose to stay above until you have cleared the set and collected the upper passage treasure; dropping early only creates extra backtracking.'],['Use the fallen ice as a path','When the upper work is finished, descend to the lower area. The fallen icicles make a new route across the gap. Cross it and inspect the side chests before taking the next exterior climb. Carry Fire/Ice protection if you have it, but keep a non-elemental damage option for the twin-headed boss.']]);
detail('c20',3,[['Save and restore at the spring','The late cave contains a recovery spring and save point. Use both before entering the next corridor. Repeatedly fighting while exhausted is unnecessary when free recovery is nearby.'],['Learn before leaving the cliff','Stilva can use Trine and Magic Breath. For each desired Enemy Skill, equip the learner before the fight and keep them alive. Do not equip an already-trained copy of that skill on the same character as an untrained copy; it blocks learning on the latter. Keep Godo alive for the fourth-copy Trine plan.']]);
detail('c20',4,[['Attack the appropriate head','Schizo’s heads have different elemental affinities. Non-elemental physical damage and summons avoid accidentally healing a head with an absorbed element. Damage one head at a time if that helps you control the finishing sequence.'],['Heal before each death retaliation','A head’s defeat triggers a final attack. Keep the group healthy before delivering the last blow, especially when the other head is still active. After the fight, finish the final exterior climb and descend toward the crater; do not leave behind the cliff’s unique treasures assuming you can return.']]);
arrival('c21','Final check before the crater’s story transition','This maze is a one-way story location. Neo Bahamut, MP Turbo, Poison Ring and the Gigas equipment/drop opportunities belong to this visit, not the later Northern Cave. Preserve a save from before completing the maze.');
detail('c21',0,[['Descend from the cliff','Follow the path down into the crater and take the stairs/rock platforms to the first broad walkway. Tifa becomes part of this story sequence, so equip her rather than assuming your previous party composition is still active.'],['Inventory check','Keep Enemy Skill available if there are remaining relevant opportunities and equip Fire defense for the coming boss. You should already have handled the cliff’s Ribbon and Trine goals; the glacier return path will not restore the full cliff dungeon afterward.']]);
detail('c21',1,[['Inspect the early ledge','Near the early save point, take the visible red Materia on the lower route for Neo Bahamut. Use the path around the rock formation to reach it; do not confuse the summon with a decorative red object.'],['Gigas collection encounters','Before advancing too far, encounter Gigas on this route. Steal Gigas Armlet for the armor collection and obtain Earth Mallet from a separate drop encounter if pursuing both. A successful steal can consume the relevant reward slot, so one enemy is not guaranteed to provide both.']]);
detail('c21',2,[['Time the first gust','Stop before the wind barrier and watch it cycle. Move only during the calm interval. If the gust hits Cloud, fight the enemy and try again rather than trying to heal through the field effect.'],['Watch later barriers for more than wind','Later crossings add moving hazards to the same timing idea. Wait for the gust and the other obstacle to create a safe gap at once. Keep your approach short so you do not overshoot into the next unsafe section.']]);
detail('c21',3,[['Prepare Fire defense','Jenova∙DEATH relies heavily on Fire damage. A Fire Ring or Elemental + Fire in linked armor slots can reduce the threat. Keep a separate healing character in case your main attacker is disabled.'],['After the battle','Complete the conversation about who will hold the Black Materia. Continue to the next path only after inspecting the ground and chests around the boss-route screens. The next dramatic scenes do not allow unlimited time for a treasure sweep afterward.']]);
detail('c21',4,[['MP Turbo and Poison Ring','Pick up MP Turbo from the field and open the Poison Ring chest along the maze route. Verify that each is in the menu before passing through the final series of story illusions and barriers.'],['A save that preserves options','Save in a new slot at the last available safe point. This is your recovery if you discover later that you skipped a unique maze item or wanted to learn Trine before losing the cliff’s access.']]);
detail('c21',5,[['Follow the story rather than backtracking','The last sequence changes the world situation and temporarily changes who you control. Finish the conversations and scripted scenes. Once the game shifts to Junon, the Highwind phase replaces the buggy/Tiny Bronco exploration phase.'],['What closed here','Early shop stock such as Shotgun, Four Slots and Mythril Clip, and the early Speed Square Umbrella prize, should already have been collected. Digital ports still follow these story-based changes even without a physical disc swap.']]);
detail('c22',0,[['Barret and Cait Sith’s escape route','Follow the changing control prompts through the press event and Junon streets. During the crisis, continue toward the airport route rather than trying to enter all of the city’s shops. The story will shift back to Tifa’s gas chamber.'],['Use the visible exits','Move through the hall and onto the upper exterior route as the escape unfolds. You are not searching for a hidden recruiting NPC; the party reunion and airship acquisition are part of the main story.']]);
detail('c22',1,[['Pick up the key','In the chamber, use Tifa’s feet to pull the dropped key within reach. The game displays body-part inputs, not the same physical button labels on every port. Follow those labels and get the key from the floor before trying to unlock her hands.'],['Release the restraints and stop the gas','Use the head/feet combination to bring the key up, then the appropriate head/hand combinations to free the wrists. Once loose, operate the gas switch at the left side. Trying the locked door alone does not complete the escape; wait for and use the opening created by the outside attack.']]);
detail('c22',2,[['Outside the chamber','Exit through the damaged wall and work down the exterior ladders. Follow the narrow route toward the cannon; the broad city streets are not your escape exit during this control segment.'],['Scarlet confrontation','At the cannon’s end, follow the slap-battle prompts. This scene does not require a special weapon, Materia or a purchased key. Finish the event and move to the rescue sequence when the route opens.']]);
detail('c22',3,[['Explore your new base','Aboard the Highwind, speak to the crew and party members. The interior operations room provides party management and the crew explains flying and landing. Open grass accepts landings; mountains, forests and many other surfaces do not.'],['First-flight detours','With Tifa leading, an extra Fort Condor defense and the conditional Nibelheim piano Elemental copy are available. Chocobo stables also open now. If you want these exact timing goals, do them before the Mideel visit advances leadership.']]);
detail('c22',4,[['Locate Mideel','Fly to the southeastern island group and land on accessible grass near the town. Enter and follow the dog/clinic conversations to find Cloud. Visit the doctor and Tifa, then return to the Highwind to finish the planning scene.'],['Optional pre-disaster key event','Before the town changes, inspect the weapon shop’s locked rear door. Search the creaking spot on the upper wooden walkway for the old key, try it at the door and admit your attempt to the shopkeeper for Curse Ring. This scene is distinct from the later Weapon steal.'],['Cid takes command','Follow the airship conversation to set Cid as leader for the first Huge Materia missions. North Corel and Fort Condor can be done in either order; the next chapters describe Corel first.']]);
detail('c23',0,[['Approach from the mountain railway','Land near North Corel and work back along the Mount Corel track toward the reactor. Save outside before triggering the Shinra departure; you want an earlier slot if the timed outcome goes poorly.'],['Prepare a fast party','Equip your strongest immediate damage, healing that does not waste many turns, and Steal for Eagle Gun’s unique Warrior Bangle. Turn off speed-boost modes if they make the lever timing difficult. You are balancing battle speed against one limited steal opportunity.']]);
detail('c23',1,[['Accelerate your engine','After the enemy train leaves, board the available engine. Alternate the lever controls indicated by the game in a steady rhythm to build speed and catch the train. Do not hold a single input continuously. The mission timer includes the later battles and braking.'],['Jump aboard','Once close enough, the party transfers to the enemy train. Move toward its front. If you fail to catch it, the mission resolves with a worse result; reload your pre-reactor save if you want the full success route.']]);
detail('c23',2,[['Clear one car at a time','Advance across the cars and finish the guard encounters promptly. Use Limits, strong summons or good physical attacks to avoid lengthy low-damage rounds. Keep someone available to heal after battle instead of starting the next encounter nearly KO’d.'],['Steal Warrior Bangle','On the Eagle Gun encounter, attempt Steal before defeating it. This is its only normal encounter window. If several attempts fail and the timer becomes untenable, the earlier save lets you retry both the steal and the train stop instead of losing one goal permanently.']]);
detail('c23',3,[['Front-car controls','At the driver’s controls, follow the on-screen lever explanation. On the original PlayStation layout, operate both levers with Up + Triangle or Down + Cross. Clear the dialogue messages with Confirm and perform the instructed lever action through the three response stages. The train briefly accelerates before the successful stop, so keep going. Match the control functions shown on your port if its physical buttons differ.'],['Do not quit at the first speed increase','The sequence includes an alarming acceleration before the final braking. Keep operating the controls through the displayed messages until the outcome is shown. Leaving the controls or assuming the first speed change means failure can waste the remaining time.']]);
detail('c23',4,[['Best outcome rewards','Stopping the train safely gives the mission’s Huge Materia, and the child in North Corel hands over Ultima without a purchase. Open the menu to verify the rewards after the celebration. Ultima starts without a usable spell until it earns its first required AP level.'],['Visit the house for Catastrophe','Speak with the woman in a North Corel house after the mission for Barret’s final Limit manual. He must learn his earlier Limits before using the manual successfully.'],['If the outcome was worse','Boarding but failing to stop can leave Ultima as an expensive purchase, while failing to board is more restrictive. The clean all-success route is to reload the pre-mission save. Once satisfied, fly to Fort Condor if that Huge Materia mission remains.']]);
detail('c24',0,[['Find the commander','Fly to the bird-topped fort south of Junon, climb through the interior and speak to the lookout commander. You can do this mission even if you skipped the earlier optional defenses. Save and equip your party before beginning.'],['Choose strategy or fallback battle','You can win with hired units or allow an enemy to reach the shack and defeat CMD. Grand Horn normally. The fallback battle is intentional and still saves the fort when won; it also offers the commander’s armor drop. Do not let a poorly equipped party lose that fallback fight.']]);
detail('c24',1,[['Strategy-battle approach','Deploy units to meet the advancing enemies, protect the climb to the shack, and move your defensive line down as the field opens. Each unit costs gil. Use the unit descriptions to counter enemies rather than covering the entire screen with static units.'],['If the enemy reaches the shack','Fight CMD. Grand Horn with your active battle party. It has a final party-wide attack as it dies, so heal before delivering the last blow. Losing is not an ordinary repeatable failure: the fort and its Huge Materia can be forfeited, making the separate save important.']]);
detail('c24',2,[['Walk outside after the scene','After winning and watching the hatching sequence, take the summit exit. Collect Phoenix from the ground outside. The summon is separate from the Huge Materia handed over inside.'],['Record the pickup','Check Summon Materia for Phoenix before leaving. If missed, Bone Village offers a later recovery route, but collecting it here avoids an unnecessary dig.']]);
detail('c24',3,[['Return to the table downstairs','Descend inside and speak directly to the old man sitting at the table. He explains the hidden Huge Materia and gives it to the party. Merely winning the battle and taking Phoenix does not complete this conversation.'],['Confirm both mission outcomes','Check Key Items and your checklist before boarding the Highwind. If Corel is still unfinished, complete that mission next. The Mideel story advances after both first missions have been resolved.']]);
detail('c24',4,[['Visit Tifa at the clinic','Once both Huge Materia missions are finished, fly back to Mideel and enter the clinic. Save before going in, since the visit leads to a fight and an extended story sequence rather than another ordinary shopping stop.'],['Prepare Steal if desired','Ultimate Weapon’s upcoming Mideel appearance offers a Curse Ring steal. Put Steal on someone now if you want that limited copy. The old-key sidequest’s ring is a separate, earlier opportunity.']]);
detail('c25',0,[['Save outside town','Make a separate save on the world map before entering the clinic. Finish the old-key event first if it is still available and you want that Curse Ring. Equip Cid’s group for a short but strong encounter.'],['Speak to Tifa and the doctor','Go into the clinic and complete the conversations. The crisis triggers through the story progression; you do not need to search elsewhere for a new sidequest NPC once both Huge Materia missions are done.']]);
detail('c25',1,[['Survive and attempt the steal','Fight Ultimate Weapon until it withdraws. Maintain HP and use good non-elemental damage. If collecting Curse Ring, attempt Steal during this encounter before it ends; later flying battles with the same Weapon do not reproduce this exact steal table.'],['Withdrawal is success here','You are not expected to kill the full late-game Weapon in Mideel. Once it leaves, follow the town disaster and the shift to Tifa’s perspective. Do not reset merely because there was no permanent Weapon-kill reward.']]);
detail('c25',2,[['Explore the memory branches','In the Lifestream area, speak to the versions of Cloud and approach each accessible memory branch. Begin with the town and mountain memories the scene presents, then return to the central area as more dialogue opens.'],['Finish the shared memories','Interact with the young Cloud and the later memory points until the sequence explains the reactor events. These are story interactions, not combat or affection checks. Continue until Cloud and Tifa return to the party.']]);
detail('c25',3,[['Cloud resumes leadership','Aboard the Highwind, finish Cloud’s account and talk to your companions. Re-form the party and redistribute equipment from Cid’s temporary group. Check that your active healer, damage options and Enemy Skill learner are all equipped.'],['New exploration opportunities','Gold Saucer racing is available again, making the standard Chocobo breeding route practical. Tifa’s Final Heaven melody and the optional mansion basement memory are also now worth revisiting. The dedicated sections provide their steps.']]);
detail('c25',4,[['Fly to Junon','The next required Huge Materia is at Junon’s underwater reactor. Land outside the lower town and use its paid elevator route to reach upper Junon. You are no longer recreating the original dolphin/parade infiltration.'],['Before the underwater facility','Carry Steal for limited soldier armor, Morph if pursuing Underwater Materia, strong Lightning and group healing for Carry Armor. Save outside the city before the long facility sequence.']]);
arrival('c26','Dock treasure comes before the submarine','Carry Armor is followed by a set of one-way dock chests. Open them before boarding. Leviathan Scales determine whether you can ever collect Oritsuru and Steal as well from Wutai’s fire cave. Save before starting the reactor mission, and again before the submarine minigame when possible.');
detail('c26',0,[['Reach upper Junon','From the lower village, use the paid elevator to reach the upper streets. Continue along the main street to the grey passage where soldiers are drilling. Follow their movement into the side route rather than continuing toward the old cargo-ship dock.'],['Follow the reactor lifts','Proceed through the military interior and use its lifts to descend. Fight the guards blocking the approach, then follow the corridor into the transparent underwater tunnel. Keep the party healed between encounters; this route ends in a much stronger boss than the ordinary soldiers.']]);
detail('c26',1,[['Guide Book opportunity','In the underwater tunnel, encounter Ghost Ship and finish it with Morph to obtain Guide Book. Morph does much less damage than a normal attack, so first lower its HP safely and only then use the finishing command. You can return for this item later if necessary.'],['Do not confuse Underwater with a story key','Guide Book is exchanged with the traveler in Kalm for Underwater Materia. That Materia removes Emerald Weapon’s timer; it is not needed to operate the reactor or win the submarine mission. Keep it as an optional endgame preparation task.']]);
detail('c26',2,[['Save before the dock confrontation','Continue through the reactor machinery to the cargo dock where Reno waits. Heal and check your Materia before approaching. Lightning is your best straightforward element; strong summons and group healing are useful as well.'],['Break Carry Armor’s arms','The arms can capture characters. Losing access to two allies makes the fight extremely dangerous, so use strong Lightning and multi-target damage to destroy the arms quickly. The body’s Lapis Laser can hit hard; keep the healer ready instead of waiting until after an ally falls.'],['Finish with a stable survivor','If a character is captured, destroying the corresponding arm frees them. Once the arms are gone, concentrate on the body while maintaining recovery. Do not enter this battle with all three characters built as low-HP casters and no item backup.']]);
detail('c26',3,[['Search before boarding','After Carry Armor, walk around the dock and inspect every chest you can reach before approaching a submarine entrance. The key treasure is Battle Trumpet, Scimitar and Leviathan Scales. Their location is outside the submarine, so inspecting the vessel’s controls will not collect them.'],['Why each pickup matters','Scimitar is Cid’s triple-growth weapon and useful for AP training. Battle Trumpet is a limited Cait Sith weapon. Leviathan Scales are a Key Item used by inspecting the flames in Wutai’s Da-chao cave; no substitute item extinguishes those flames.'],['Last armor checks','If you want Shinra Alpha, use Steal on the relevant SOLDIER:1st encounters in this facility before leaving the sequence. Keep this goal separate from the ship’s earlier Shinra Beta armor.']]);
detail('c26',4,[['Board and learn the controls','Enter the grey submarine and resolve its guard encounters. Read the minigame controls carefully before launching. The mission asks you to sink the red submarine carrying the Huge Materia, not every target in the ocean.'],['Attack the red target promptly','The red submarine begins directly ahead. Bring it into your sights and fire torpedoes while pursuing; avoid wasting the timer on unrelated targets. If the mission fails and you are preserving all four successful Huge Materia outcomes, reload the pre-minigame save.']]);
detail('c26',5,[['Dive to the red wreck','After you gain free submarine control, travel to the southern part of the sea near the island chain and dive. Inspect the red submarine wreck on the seabed to collect the cargo. The game does not add the Huge Materia merely because you won the torpedo battle.'],['Know your new exploration options','The submarine also reaches the Sunken Gelnika, the northern underwater key tunnel and the passage toward Lucrecia’s cave. You can explore before the rocket mission; the main story next points to Rocket Town and Cid.']]);
detail('c27',0,[['Add Cid before the rocket','Fly to Rocket Town and include Cid in your active party. Enter the town, walk to the rocket and climb the exterior route. The Shinra soldiers blocking the climb must be defeated before you enter.'],['Prepare Steal','The Rude fight before boarding has a limited Ziedrich opportunity. Put Steal on an active character and leave enough party healing to survive repeated attempts. Cid’s story participation does not automatically supply the gear you moved elsewhere earlier.']]);
detail('c27',1,[['Separate the guards from Rude','Defeat the accompanying soldiers while keeping the party healthy, then concentrate on Rude. If collecting Ziedrich, secure the steal before ending the encounter. The Gelnika and Midgar provide other limited copies, not an unlimited armor shop.'],['Proceed into the rocket','Once the way is clear, enter the capsule and follow the launch sequence. Continue talking to Cid and the crew until Cloud can explore the interior again.']]);
detail('c27',2,[['Climb to the upper compartment','Inside the rocket in space, use the ladder leading to the Materia security room. Inspect the container and start entering a sequence. You must do this before leaving the rocket; the later escape is not a return route to this room.'],['Use a pre-entry save as your fallback','If the security attempt runs out before the lock opens, the clean collection fix is the earlier Rocket Town save. Randomly trying codes consumes the available time and is unnecessary when the exact function sequence is known.']]);
detail('c27',3,[['Command-function sequence','Enter Confirm → Switch → Cancel → Cancel. On the original PlayStation this is Circle → Square → Cross → Cross. Ports and custom controller mappings can swap the physical buttons, so match the function labels rather than assuming a modern controller’s confirm button is Circle.'],['Verify the reward','The container’s Huge Materia can represent an earlier failed mission if one was missed. Four successful missions produce the normal full set, including the blue Huge Materia needed for the observatory’s usual Bahamut ZERO route. Collecting one in the rocket does not undo every possible earlier mission failure.']]);
detail('c27',4,[['Return to the main compartment','After the lock reward, descend from the Materia room and follow Cid through the rocket. The blocked escape is resolved through Shera’s scene; keep following the story interactions rather than looking for another code.'],['Escape pod','Reach the pod, interact with its controls and finish the return-to-planet sequence. When free flight resumes, land near Cosmo Canyon to discuss what comes next with Bugenhagen.']]);
detail('c27',5,[['Store the Huge Materia','Climb to the observatory and speak to Bugenhagen. Follow the storage scene, then inspect the individual Huge Materia as desired. If you have all four plus Bahamut and Neo Bahamut, examine the blue one for Bahamut ZERO.'],['Plan the next submarine trip','Bugenhagen points toward the Forgotten Capital and an ancient key beneath the sea. The next chapter covers the northern underwater tunnel. You can still pause for Chocobo breeding, Gelnika treasure and optional character stories before returning to Midgar.']]);
detail('c28',0,[['Find the northern underwater passage','Take the submarine to the northern sea and dive. Look for the underwater tunnel opening in the northern rock wall rather than a surface beach or the red submarine wreck. Follow the long narrow passage to its far end.'],['Pick up the Key to the Ancients','At the end of the tunnel, approach the large key-shaped object and interact with it. Verify it appears in Key Items, then reverse through the passage and surface where there is room. It is not ordinary Materia and does not require Morph.']]);
detail('c28',1,[['Return by air','Use the Highwind to travel back to the northern continent and approach the Forgotten Capital. Bugenhagen accompanies the story visit. From the capital’s entrance junction, take the western/left branch toward the large shell-like mechanism.'],['Reach the center of the device','Follow the left-side path and descend into the interior where Bugenhagen waits. Speak with him and inspect the mechanism rather than returning to the altar used at the end of Disc 1.']]);
detail('c28',2,[['Use the key through the scene','With the Key to the Ancients in inventory, finish Bugenhagen’s conversation and follow the interaction at the device. The resulting waterfall image/memory explains the next objective. You do not equip the key or cast a spell to activate it.'],['Before leaving the north','This is a useful checkpoint for saving and reviewing unfinished side quests. Optional story scenes such as the mansion memory and Vincent’s cave can still be completed now, and the Gelnika Turks still need to be visited before the Midgar raid ends if you want their encounter.']]);
detail('c28',3,[['Leave and follow the crisis','Return to the Highwind and finish the new world-event scenes. Diamond Weapon is moving toward Midgar on the eastern continent. Fly to the open ground near its path and land before trying to make contact.'],['Prepare on foot','You initiate this Weapon encounter by touching it with the party on the world map, not by ramming it with the airship. Open the menu and configure magic, summons and Steal before making contact.']]);
detail('c28',4,[['Save and steal reminder','Make a separate save outside Midgar. Diamond Weapon carries Rising Sun, a unique steal for Yuffie. Put Steal on an active character now; after the Weapon is defeated, that opportunity is gone.'],['Battle preparation','Use magic and summons to bypass its closed-core physical immunity. Carry Echo Screens or status protection for Silence and enough healing to recover from its countdown attack. The next chapter details the battle and the raid setup.']]);
detail('c29',0,[['Closed-core phase','While Diamond Weapon’s core is closed, ordinary physical attacks are ineffective. Use Lightning magic, non-elemental summons and other reliable magical damage. Do not waste repeated attacks simply because Cloud’s strongest weapon is equipped.'],['Steal Rising Sun first','Attempt Steal until you obtain Rising Sun before finishing the battle. Keep one or two other characters healing or defending during repeated attempts. This is the only normal source of this weapon.']]);
detail('c29',1,[['The countdown changes its state','When the boss begins the countdown, its core opens and physical attacks become effective. Use that opportunity for Limits and strong normal attacks, but avoid taking the party’s HP too low while chasing damage.'],['Recover after Diamond Flash','Diamond Flash deals heavy proportional damage and can Silence characters. Cure the status on your healer with an Echo Screen or another reliable item, then restore HP. Keep a healthy character free to act before resuming an all-out attack cycle.']]);
detail('c29',2,[['Return to the Highwind','After winning, reboard the airship and let the world-event scenes finish. The game opens the Midgar raid objective after the cannon crisis. You can still choose to make optional stops before flying over the city.'],['Review time-limited detours','Finish Wutai’s Materia-theft rescue before completing the coming raid if you want its scenes. Visit the Gelnika Turks now if you want their encounter and steals. These have different deadlines from the Gelnika’s treasure, which remains accessible later.']]);
detail('c29',3,[['Keep a pre-raid save','Save in a separate slot on the world map before approaching Midgar from the air. The raid contains several one-visit treasure areas and multiple boss fights; this save is your recovery if you later notice a missing weapon.'],['Equip for a long sequence','Bring good healing, revival, status cures and Steal for the Turks. Have Barret ready for the later stairs even if he is not your usual main attacker. You can change your party at the available save points, but must remember to do so before his weapon chest.']]);
detail('c29',4,[['Initiate the drop','Fly the Highwind over Midgar and follow the party’s parachute plan. On landing, talk to Cait Sith and follow him to the hatch leading into the maintenance platforms.'],['This is a different city route','The raid does not give unrestricted access to all old slums. Follow the maintenance route, subway tunnels, optional Shinra HQ branch and cannon approach described in the next chapter.']]);
arrival('c30','Do these three things before the final stairs','Explore the underground maintenance detours, make the optional Shinra HQ return, and put Barret in the active party before the Missing Score chest. Going straight after Cait Sith can skip valuable one-time equipment. The warning register has separate checks for each named reward.');
detail('c30',0,[['Use the first save and inspect the platforms','Follow Cait Sith down the hatch, then save. The maintenance screens contain stairs, ladders, a collapsing walkway and lower-level branches. Do not treat the first ladder pointing forward as proof that every other ladder is decorative.'],['First-screen side treasure','Explore the reachable branches for Elixir and Megalixir before committing down the main maintenance route. Keep track of where you can climb back up; the area’s apparent height changes make simple left/right directions insufficient without following the ladders.'],['Aegis Armlet detour','At the lower platform junction, take the left-side ladder/branch that returns toward an upper isolated chest for Aegis Armlet. Return to the junction afterward. Check the item name in the treasure message instead of assuming a nearby ordinary consumable was the armor.'],['Starlight M-phone and Max Ray','Explore the remaining connected platform chests for Starlight M-phone. Take the long service-passage detour leading to the far isolated chest for Max Ray before using the ventilation exit into the railway tunnels. These weapons cannot be cleaned up by revisiting Midgar after the raid.']]);
detail('c30',1,[['Go opposite the apparent story direction','On entering the long subway tunnel, the main story lies north/up-screen. For W-Item, deliberately travel south/down-screen through repeated tunnel sections. Party dialogue confirms the long detour; keep going until the dead-end pickup.'],['Claim W-Item and return','Collect the yellow W-Item Materia at the far end, plus accessible consumables along the detour. Retrace the repeated screens north to the original junction. If you miss W-Item here, a Bone Village dig can recover it, but the raid pickup is simpler.']]);
detail('c30',2,[['Steal before ending the battle','If fighting the Turks, steal Minerva Band from Elena, Touph Ring from Reno and Ziedrich from Rude before finishing any one of them. When one falls, the others retreat, which can end the remaining steal chances.'],['Peaceful outcome is a conscious choice','Completing Wutai’s rescue may allow the group to part without fighting. That choice gives the peaceful resolution and skips this encounter’s steals. Keep the pre-raid save if you want to preserve both possibilities; one choice cannot yield both versions of the scene.']]);
detail('c30',3,[['Follow the building branch before the cannon route','At the tunnel forks, inspect the available branch signs and choose the path leading toward Shinra HQ before advancing toward the cannon. If you reach the building’s lower interior, you have found the optional detour; you are not supposed to repeat the old reactor missions.'],['Lobby flyer · final chance','Read Turtle’s Paradise #2 in the first-floor lobby if it is not already checked. This is the last return to the building. Missing it now prevents the six-flyer set even though the other flyer locations remain accessible.'],['Second-floor chests','Return to the item shop area you could not fully loot during the first visit. Open the two chests for Master Fist and Pile Banger. The old locked-chest situation has changed; no separate key-hunting quest is required.'],['Upper-floor sweep','Visit floor 63 for Grow Lance and floor 64’s locker room for HP Shout. On the first visit Cloud rejected the megaphone as too large; now Cait Sith’s weapon can be taken. Also inspect the long stairwell for Behemoth Horn. Its availability does not require having left the early Elixir uncollected.'],['Return to the subway','After the treasure sweep, leave the building by the route you entered and return to the tunnel branches. Continue toward the streets/cannon instead of walking the same HQ stairs repeatedly. Verify the four return-only weapon checks before moving on.']]);
detail('c30',4,[['Save before the machine','On reaching the streets, continue through the encounter approach until Proud Clod blocks progress. Heal before triggering it. Strong multi-target damage can break its supporting armor while damaging the body.'],['Proud Clod strategy','Keep HP high for the machine’s powerful attacks. Defensive magic and reliable group healing are more valuable than trying to exploit an uncertain elemental weakness. Destroy the armor if needed, then finish the main body. The victory awards Ragnarok.'],['Continue to the staircase save','After the machine falls, collect the accessible treasure and move toward the long cannon stairs. Use the next save opportunity before the final ascent, and prepare Barret now rather than after the boss scene begins.']]);
detail('c30',5,[['Set Barret in the active three','Change the battle party at a permitted save point or through the available party-management option before climbing toward Hojo. Merely having Barret recruited is insufficient; he must be in the active group for the Missing Score chest to appear.'],['Open the staircase chest','Climb the long metal staircase in the rain and inspect the chest on the route before the final confrontation. Take Missing Score and verify it in Barret’s equipment list. If there is no chest, return to a permitted party-change point and add him before advancing.']]);
detail('c30',6,[['Save and status protection','Restore the party’s HP and MP before the last approach. Equip Ribbons or relevant status accessories and ensure revival is not concentrated on only one fragile character. Hojo’s battle has three consecutive forms.'],['Three-form strategy','In the first form, focus the main enemy rather than indefinitely clearing assistants. Continue strong damage and healing through the transforming middle form. In the last form, cure the status effects from its repeated combo promptly and maintain defensive buffs as needed.'],['Disc 2 closes','After winning, finish the long party and world-event scenes. Disc 3 leaves the world largely open for final preparations, but the underground raid, Shinra HQ treasure and Wutai theft window cannot be replayed freely. Keep the pre-raid save even after making a new post-raid one.']]);
detail('c31',0,[['Re-form the final party','Speak with the companions after the airship scenes and choose your preferred group. Equip armor and accessories first, then distribute healing, revival, status cures and damage across more than one character. High-level offensive magic is of little help if a single Silence disables every useful action.'],['Growth versus ultimate weapons','Many ultimate weapons have no Materia growth. Use double- or triple-growth equipment while training, then switch to the weapon best suited to the boss. Cid’s Scimitar and Cloud’s Apocalypse are valuable AP tools if collected.']]);
detail('c31',1,[['Recruit anyone still missing','Yuffie remains in forest encounters and Vincent remains behind the mansion-safe/basement sequence. If you followed the early route, both should already be available; if not, the Characters section gives the exact recruitment steps.'],['Do the optional story visits','Return with Cloud to the mansion laboratory for the optional memory. Take Vincent to Lucrecia’s cave, fight at least ten battles and return for his rewards. Visit Bugenhagen with Red XIII for Limited Moon. These are substantial scenes easily missed by flying straight to the crater.'],['Choose your challenges','Complete Chocobo breeding and the four Materia caves, explore the Gelnika and Ancient Forest, earn Battle Square rewards, or fight Emerald and Ruby. None of these is required merely to reach the ending, so treat the checklist as a set of chosen goals rather than a forced grind.']]);
detail('c31',2,[['Review permanent-loss records','Open Items & events and filter to Permanent. Mark what you actually obtained or missed; viewing this late chapter does not let the guide inspect your game or infer losses. Missing Score, HP Shout, the temple summons and early shop stock should be checked against your inventory.'],['Resolve the fourth-copy Trine plan','The fourth Enemy Skill is with the Chocobo Sage. If Godo is still alive, equip Yuffie only with the copies that lack Trine and let him cast it before winning. A trained copy equipped on the same learner prevents the untrained ones learning that skill.']]);
detail('c31',3,[['Keep an external save','Save outside the crater in its own slot before starting the final dungeon. Carry Ethers/Turbo Ethers, Phoenix Downs and your strongest recovery items. You can return from much of the cave, but an independent outside save protects against a bad Save Crystal placement or an accidental final commitment.'],['Optional survival combinations','Final Attack linked to Phoenix can revive the group after its wearer is KO’d, provided the wearer has enough MP and remaining uses. Do not assume the pairing is infinite or automatically works merely because both Materia are somewhere in the equipment.']]);
detail('c31',4,[['Enter from the Highwind','Fly to the crater in the northern continent and approach the large opening. The party disembarks at the rim, where you can begin the descending path. Recheck the active group before climbing down.'],['One-time Enemy Skill warning','Before the right-hand graveyard route, save and equip the Enemy Skill copies you want Pandora’s Box on. Treat the first Dragon Zombie death as your only opportunity. The detailed cave chapter separates each branch so you can plan the pickup and this encounter.']]);
arrival('c32','Explore first, commit later','The cave has a first left/right split and another split on the left route. All branches contain worthwhile treasure. For a straightforward complete sweep, explore one route to the meeting area, backtrack to the fork, then check the others before taking the final downward leap.');
detail('c32',0,[['Crater rim and Save Crystal','Open the first chest for Save Crystal and take the descending spiral path. The cave mouth along the upper route leads back out; remember it if returning to the Highwind. Check the spiral’s small branches for sources and restorative items before moving into the next chamber.'],['Rock-ledge chamber','Use the ledges to descend through the chamber with multiple cave openings. Take side passages for the treasure chests, including HP Absorb, before following the lower exit. Some ledges are reached by dropping from above rather than trying to climb directly from the bottom.'],['Save Crystal placement','The crystal creates one save point where used. Keep an outside save and place it only on flat, safe ground away from ladders or transitions. Do not use it merely because the first menu after entering offers the option.']]);
detail('c32',1,[['First split: right route','The right route leads into the graveyard/dragon area. This branch contains valuable equipment, including Mystile, and the dangerous Dragon Zombie encounter. Before entering, equip your intended Pandora’s Box learners and make an independent save.'],['Pandora’s Box protocol','The first defeated Dragon Zombie attempts the skill as a final attack. Keep learners alive and the enemy’s MP intact. Do not drain its MP to make the battle safer, because a failed cast can waste the unique opportunity. Reload if the learning you want does not occur.'],['First split: left route','The left side splits again into an upper watery route and a lower rocky route. Explore both. Party members sent down other routes may hand you items at the meeting area, but their finds are not a substitute for physically checking every branch.']]);
detail('c32',2,[['Left upper: Shield and the underwater path','On the upper watery route, follow the rocks to the green Shield Materia on its raised platform. Walking downward from that platform takes Cloud through the water to a lower chest, including Imperial Guard. Check the apparent dead-end rock edges for these automatic swimming transitions.'],['Left upper: W-Magic and Counter','In the glowing chamber beyond, inspect the top foliage for W-Magic and the bright central area for Counter. Both can blend into the scenery. Counter here is Support Materia linked to a command; it is different from Counter Attack and from Magic Counter.'],['Left lower: Mega All','On the rocky route, inspect the ledge where Cloud automatically jumps between platforms. Press Confirm at the moment he passes the Mega All pickup. If missed, repeat the jump and try again. Open the nearby restorative-item chests before continuing.'],['Right route: Magic Counter','On the right branch, examine the glowing mako/wall area for Magic Counter rather than searching only treasure chests. Continue the branch treasure sweep before returning to the gathering point.']]);
detail('c32',3,[['The swamp AP area','The watery left-upper route is a strong training location. Magic Pots award good AP after you give each an Elixir and defeat it; attacking before satisfying the request is ineffective. Movers are rare but particularly valuable AP encounters.'],['Train the Materia that will matter','Equip growth weapons and armor intentionally; zero-growth equipment earns no Materia AP. Level your healing, support and core damage tools first. If you have no Elixirs to spare, choose other encounters instead of waiting in front of an unsatisfied Magic Pot.']]);
detail('c32',4,[['Talk to everyone','At the bottom gathering area, speak to each companion to receive their exploration finds. Recheck your equipment and collect any remaining branch treasures before initiating the final descent. You may still backtrack from this meeting area.'],['Return path if needed','Use the upper route out of the gathering chamber to climb back through the explored branches to the earlier fork, then continue back up the ledges and spiral to the rim. If you cannot find an exit, use Assist and look for the high cave doorway rather than repeatedly dropping farther down.']]);
detail('c32',5,[['Final loadout','Set Ribbons/status protection, reliable healing, resurrection and a strong damage method. Restore HP and MP before agreeing to go on. If the final battle uses extra parties, give those characters at least functional equipment instead of leaving every useful Materia on three people.'],['Point of no return','Once you take the final downward commitment beyond the party gathering, the end sequence runs through the last encounters and bosses. Keep the earlier external save to return to side quests afterward; there is no ordinary walk back to the world during the ending.']]);
detail('c33',0,[['Final approach encounters','Work through the last stepping-stone encounters on the way to Jenova. Heal between fights when the menu is available. You cannot rely on returning to a town after these battles, so use your stocked restorative items instead of preserving them indefinitely.'],['Jenova∙SYNTHESIS countdown','Focus the main body; destroy or control the arms when their interference threatens your healer. When the boss begins its final countdown, use your strongest damage to finish before Ultima. If you cannot, enter that moment with HP and defenses restored.']]);
detail('c33',1,[['Understand the parts','Bizarro∙Sephiroth has multiple body parts and a core that is protected until supporting parts are handled. Attack the exposed parts to change the state, then damage the core and main body when possible. Hitting a protected core repeatedly does not solve the phase.'],['Multiple-party variation','Your playthrough can change how many groups participate. Follow the switch prompts and defeat the relevant parts in each group if needed. Keep healing available on the party you switch to, rather than assuming it inherits the first group’s spells.']]);
detail('c33',2,[['Establish recovery and tempo','At Safer∙Sephiroth, keep the healer able to act and restore defensive buffs when they wear off or are removed. Haste helps, but immediate recovery after a large attack takes priority over rebuffing an already stable party.'],['Damage during safe windows','Use strong non-elemental summons, high-damage Limits and your best physical attacks when the boss is reachable. If it rises out of ordinary melee reach, use ranged or magical options instead of spending ineffective turns on Attack.']]);
detail('c33',3,[['Recover from the animation','Super Nova’s long animation ends in heavy proportional damage and status pressure. It is a cue to heal and cure, not proof that a full-HP party has necessarily lost the fight. Use items from unaffected characters if the primary healer is disabled.'],['Do not let statuses cascade','Remove Confusion, Silence and other disabling effects promptly. Ribbon helps prevent many of them. If two allies fall, stabilize with revival and healing before chasing another big damage turn; a surviving recovery character is more important than a nearly charged Limit on someone KO’d.']]);
detail('c33',4,[['Cloud’s final confrontation','After the main victory, follow the remaining scene into Cloud’s final solo encounter. The game supplies the intended final command; use the available Limit rather than searching for a special item or a hidden equipment requirement.'],['Watch beyond the credits','Let the ending and credits complete to see the final follow-up scene. Completing the walkthrough’s checks records your playthrough goals, not a new postgame world state written into your game save.']]);
detail('c33',5,[['Preserve the journal','Use the journal button to export your progress, notes, item/event statuses, character checks and Chocobo records. Keep the external game save too; the guide’s JSON is only a checklist backup.'],['Return to unfinished goals','Load your pre-finale game save for remaining breeding, superbosses or collection work. Use the guide’s relevant chapter or quest rather than resetting its progress unless you actually want a new checklist.']]);
SOURCES.push(['Corel train controls','Original control combinations for the braking sequence','https://jegged.com/Games/Final-Fantasy-VII/Walkthrough/Disc-2/31-Mount-Corel.html'],['Northern Cave reference','Branch-specific treasure and return-path cross-check','https://jegged.com/Games/Final-Fantasy-VII/Walkthrough/Disc-3/39-Northern-Cave.html']);
// Additional chapter inventories. Existing entries keep their indices for saved progress.
